rules_version = '2';
// Widebed PMS Firestore rules. Draft 0.47, 10 Nov 2026: Issues <-> TMS Maintenance link. Directors and the tagged roles can
// change a ticket's title, description and property (its card is on that property's board in the TMS), and its tmsStatus (the task system column the ticket's card is in, a map
// { name, for }), with or without a status change, while it is Open or In progress. The task system (TMS) writes these as
// the signed-in person, with their own PMS sign-in, so the same people can change the same tickets. Mark completed through
// this rule also needs doneByUid == the person. Nothing else changes; Completed tickets stay locked.
// Draft 0.46, 6 Nov 2026 (Khairul): Pool Sharing check on Month-end: Accounting / Directors save
// "Confirmed 0 bookings" on a month document (poolZero only). Month summaries (unitMonths) may hold
// 'arrangementType'. Fee arrangements need no change: they are saved on the property's rateVersions, which Accounting /
// Directors already create.
// Draft 0.45, 5 Nov 2026 (Khairul): HR can make a salary advance form for a staff member
// (advances byHR: created straight at Reviewed, within 50% of their salary, not interns, never for themselves), with the form
// and the signature-use line in the same save. The staff member reads it but can't sign it in the PMS (paper only; HR marks it
// signed outside). Also (6 Nov 2026): the Procurement Forms page is removed, so procurementForms.view leaves the procurement preset.
// Also (6 Nov 2026): SOPs get an icon (a short icon name HR picks).
// Also (6 Nov 2026): HR and Directors can delete an SOP: a soft delete (deleted: true with a reason), the record stays.
// Also (6 Nov 2026): HR can make new SOPs (sops/{key}: any lower-case key with dashes, with a title and short line), not only the first four.
// Also (6 Nov 2026): issues get a type (customer or inhouse); Directors and the tagged roles can change it while the ticket is open or in progress.
// Draft 0.44, 5 Nov 2026 (Khairul): salary advance requests no longer need a "needed by" date
// (the field is optional; older requests keep theirs). Nothing else changes.
// Draft 0.43, 5 Nov 2026 (Khairul): salary advance review no longer asks how the Director was
// told (the tick alone, saved with HR's name and time). Only the chloeTold.how check is removed. Nothing else changes.
// Draft 0.42, 5 Nov 2026 (Khairul): Salary advances (0.41 was never published; this replaces it).
// staffHR/{uid} (IC, position, salary) and advanceLimits/{uid} (50% of salary, same save): HR and Directors write; HR can't
// change their own. The person reads only their own limit. Interns (users/{uid}.intern) can't ask for an advance.
// advances/{id}: staff create their own (Submitted, amount <= 50% of the salary in staffHR), read their own, withdraw while
// Submitted, and sign once Reviewed (signed/main, drawn or uploaded). HR (never on their own request): Review (amount, Director
// told; frozen form advances/{id}/form/main + signatureUses/{id} in the same batch), mark signed outside the PMS (fully signed
// document signed/copy required), add or replace signed/copy later, Approve (pending payment), Paid (payment type, date,
// screenshot payment/main), Reject at Submitted or Signed. form and signed: the staff member, HR and Directors read; payment:
// HR and Directors only. advances/{id}/notes: HR writes, HR and Directors read. signatures/director: HR and Directors.
// counters/advances for SA- refs. Nothing is deleted. Nothing else changes.
// Draft 0.40, 5 Nov 2026 (Khairul): second fix for 0.38. HR still couldn't read the private
// part (subject, details) of their own Director complaint. dirSide() now reads the complaint and the role once each, the
// private-part rule is split into separate lines, and a backup line lets HR read a private part whose fromUid is theirs.
// Nothing else changes.
// Draft 0.39, 5 Nov 2026 (Khairul): fix for 0.38. HR's "my Director complaints" list
// (kind == director, fromId == me) was refused because the read rule used get('fromId', null), which a list query can't
// be checked against. It now compares resource.data.fromId directly. Nothing else changes.
// Draft 0.38, 5 Nov 2026 (Khairul): Director complaints are private to the HR person who sent
// them. A new Director complaint keeps the sender's uid (fromId) on the main record; HR reads only their own Director
// complaints (record, private part, conversation, photos) and replies only on those. Directors still read all. Staff
// complaints unchanged (HR reads all). Nothing else changes.
// Draft 0.37, 5 Nov 2026 (Khairul): HR Announcements. announcements/{id}: anyone signed in reads
// the ones meant for their role or Everyone; HR and Directors read all, post, edit and delete. announcements/{id}/views/{uid}:
// written once by that person (first time they open it), read by that person, HR and Directors. announcementReads/{uid}: the
// person's own list of opened announcements, only they read and write it. Files go to Google Drive, not Firestore. Nothing else changes.
// Draft 0.36, 5 Nov 2026 (Khairul): delete a cancelled offline booking for good. Accounting,
// Directors and Operations may delete an offlineBookings document whose status is 'cancelled', with its private part and
// its utility bill (utilityBills/{same id}). Cancelling itself needed no change. Nothing else changes.
// Draft 0.35, 5 Nov 2026 (Khairul, on top of Neo's Draft 0.34 below): joint owners. An owner's
// private part may hold coOwners (extra owners' names and contact details), so Operations (adding an owner) and Marketing
// (editing names and contact details) may write it too. Nothing else changes.
// Draft 0.34, 4 Nov 2026 (Neo, on top of Khairul's Draft 0.33 below): COH questions added
// mid-quarter. An evaluator who already submitted (even if HR/Director approved it) can add answers to the new
// questions; the evaluation goes back to 'submitted' for review. Once approved, the scores document can only grow
// (earlier answers can't be removed). Nothing else changes.
// Draft 0.33, 4 Nov 2026 (Khairul, on top of Neo's Draft 0.32 below): puts back Khairul's
// Draft 0.30 and 0.31, which were missing from 0.32: the Directors set a Director complaint's status (Read by the Directors /
// In review / Closed, closing note in the conversation, HR can't reply once Closed), the Directors' own notes
// (complaints/{id}/notes on a 'director' complaint, Directors only), and the sender's uid (fromUid) on a complaint's
// private part for the profile picture. Also fixes the What's New rule (updates/{id}), whose first line had been cut
// to the top of the file. Nothing else changes.
// Draft 0.32, 4 Nov 2026: every staff member can do COH and KPI self-rating.
// (1) cohEvaluations/{id}/private/scores: read/create/update no longer call get() on a parent that may not exist
// yet (first "Evaluate" probe, and the batch that creates the evaluation + its scores together). get() on a missing
// document errors, and an error means deny, so only roles with another way in (Director, HR, Finance via the
// private catch-all) could evaluate. Create now uses existsAfter/getAfter; read allows the not-found probe.
// (2) The private catch-all no longer covers cohEvaluations, so Finance can't read other people's COH marks.
// (3) kpiConversations / kpiDiscussions reads get the same (resource == null && anyStaff()) probe guard.
// Draft 0.31, 4 Nov 2026 (Neo): KPI Director Review workflow—
// kpiSubmissions enhanced with director review fields (directorRating, directorComments, discussionStatus,
// discussionHistory, discussionThreadId). Employee can resubmit/discuss while director can send back,
// re-rate, or approve. Discussion threads in kpiDiscussions/{id} allow back-and-forth before final approval.
// Draft 0.30, 4 Nov 2026 (merge): Khairul's Draft 0.29 (Director complaint
// threads/photos) rebased onto a snapshot that predated six read-rule fixes from earlier the same day — those
// are reapplied here. The bug: cohEvaluations/kpiAssignments/kpiSubmissions/performanceDiscussions/
// performanceTmsSnapshots/performanceResults all checked resource.data.<field> without first handling
// resource == null. Firestore errors out evaluating .data on a null resource (i.e. the document doesn't exist
// yet), and a rule error means deny — so any getDoc() probing "does this exist yet" (a brand-new KPI task, an
// evaluation that hasn't happened yet, etc.) got permission-denied instead of a normal "not found." Each of
// the six now starts with (resource == null && anyStaff()) || so that probe is allowed through safely; no
// other access was widened. PULL BEFORE EDITING, same as always — this file is edited by both Khairul and Neo.
// Draft 0.29, 4 Nov 2026 (Khairul): Director complaints (HR to the Directors) get the same
// conversation and photos: HR and Directors read and write complaints/{id}/thread and /images of a 'director' complaint.
// Draft 0.28, 4 Nov 2026 (Khairul, on top of Neo's Draft 0.26 below): staff complaint follow-up
// and photos put back (they were Khairul's 0.26 / 0.27 and missing from Neo's copy): HR sets Read by HR / In review / Closed;
// complaints/{id}/thread (HR and the NAMED sender write, the sender reads); complaints/{id}/notes (HR only);
// complaints/{id}/images (one shrunk photo each, read like the conversation). Nothing in them is ever edited or deleted.
// PULL BEFORE EDITING: this file is edited by both Khairul and Neo, and the last publish wins.
// Draft 0.26, 4 Nov 2026 (Neo): COH evaluation marks are no longer on the evaluatee-readable
// cohEvaluations document — they live in a private/scores sub-document only the evaluator and HR/Director can read,
// so the person being rated never sees the exact score a specific colleague gave them (evaluator identity stays
// visible, by the existing confirmed business rule).
// Draft 0.25, 4 Nov 2026 (Khairul): HR opening a New staff complaint marks it Read by HR (status 'read').
// Draft 0.24, 4 Nov 2026 (Khairul, on top of Neo's Draft 0.23 below): push notifications
// (pushTokens/{token}, one per device, written and read only by the person signed in there; api/push.js reads them with the
// service account) and Finance/Director may permanently delete a booking that was removed by hand on Month-end.
// Draft 0.23, 3 Nov 2026 (Neo): Performance Management Stage 1 + Stage 2 (audit
// remediation): performanceQuarters update is split into a draft-only full-edit branch, a status-only
// lifecycle-advance branch, and a Director-only finalized->pendingApproval reopen branch, so a quarter's
// config can't be changed once it leaves draft. performanceResults no longer has an unconditional Director
// bypass alongside the finalized check (the two branches were OR'd, so the bypass made the check meaningless);
// there is now exactly one non-finalized write condition, plus one deliberate, revision-tracked correction
// path (Director only, straight from 'finalized', revisionNumber+1, reason + corrector required) paired with
// an immutable performanceResults/{id}/revisions/{rev} snapshot of the pre-correction values. kpiSubmissions'
// employee branch no longer accepts a write once the submission is already approved or rejected, so an
// employee can't reset a reviewed submission back to 'submitted' to erase the reviewer's decision. (This
// reapplies Draft "Stage 1" fixes that were dropped when this file was rebased from an older snapshot while
// Draft 0.21/0.22 notification work landed — see PERFORMANCE_MANAGEMENT_HANDOFF.md.)
// Draft 0.22, 3 Nov 2026: Notifications page clean-up: the recipient may delete a notification
// sent to them personally, and hide a team (role) notification for themselves only (hiddenBy).
// Draft 0.21, 3 Nov 2026 (Khairul + Neo combined): Neo's merge (below) plus Khairul's
// Draft 0.21: notifications may go to roles made on the Roles page (roles/{id} exists), not only the 7 built-in roles.
// Neo's merge, 3 Nov 2026: base Draft 0.20, with two fixes restored from the stale root firestore.rules (agreement
// renewals staff-read on users/{uid}, agreementLinks delete support), PLUS the new Performance Management collections.
// firebase.json deploys THIS file (firebase/firestore.rules). The root firestore.rules is stale and not deployed.
//
// Draft 0.20, 3 Nov 2026: ticket quotes and invoices (issueQuotes/{ticketId}: anyone on the ticket adds and reads
// the quote, Director and Expenses Edit approve and add it to the owner's unit expenses). Draft 0.19, 3 Nov 2026:
// What's New page (updates/{id}: every staff member reads, Director posts, edits, deletes). Draft 0.18, 3 Nov 2026:
// owner payment status on statements (Pending Payment / Paid, Invoices & Receipts), no reopen once Paid, Director
// can delete an unused custom role. Draft 0.18, 2 Nov 2026 (restored from root firestore.rules): agreement renewals
// — every staff member may read the staff list (names for the "In charge" picker on agreements).
// Draft 0.17, 2 Nov 2026: roles/{id} (Roles page: new roles and changed usual pages, Director only), myPerms reads
// them. Draft 0.17, 30 Oct 2026 (restored from root firestore.rules): fill-in links can be deleted (agreementLinks).
// Draft 0.16, 30 Oct 2026: Neo's Draft 0.15 (agreement master files, fill-in links, 'submitted' record status) plus
// booking numbers (lodgmentCounters), the Willow booking import into offlineBookings,
// and Operations editing booking details (reservationLodgments rules removed).
// Offline payments: Operations may view the page (preset) and fill in a payment with status Unknown, which becomes Edited; an Offline Payments View tick no longer opens the other finance data.
// Draft 0.14, 30 Oct 2026: Draft 0.13 plus Agreements (forms, templates, records, views,
// generated PDFs). Every staff member fills in agreement forms and reads every record. Forms and templates change only with
// the "Agreement Setup" tick (Directors always). Files (PDFs, IC copies) are in Google Drive, not Firestore.
// Draft 0.13, 29 Oct 2026: Draft 0.12 (page access, Neo) plus utilityBills and booking door passcodes.
// users/{uid}.perms (ticked on Staff accounts) lists the pages a person may view or edit: '<page>.view' / '<page>.edit'.
// No perms saved = the role's preset (presetFor below), so accounts that were never changed behave as in Draft 0.10.
// Data is protected per area: any Finance page opens the finance data, Portfolio Edit opens owners/units/terms, and so on.
// Directors keep everything. Statement approvals, Director Override, brand logos, staff accounts, the audit log and
// complaints still follow the role only and can't be ticked.
// Draft 0.10, 27 Oct 2026: (1) notifications: an anonymous complaint alert to HR may be created with no sender (createdByUid null);
// (2) complaints: staff complaints are readable by HR only (Directors keep Director complaints).
// 27 Oct (Khairul): Marketing may add and edit properties, units and owners (no money/bank) and edit New Owner Listings.
// History: 0.34 COH new questions after submitting. 0.33 Director complaint status/notes, fromUid, What's New fix.
// 0.32 COH/KPI for every staff member (null-safe scores rules, Finance no longer reads COH marks).
// 0.30 six resource==null read-rule fixes reapplied. 0.29 Director complaint threads/photos. 0.28 staff
// complaint thread/photos/notes. 0.26 COH marks moved to a private sub-document (evaluatee can't read scores).
// 0.25 HR complaint read-marking.
// 0.24 push notifications; Finance/Director delete a hand-removed booking. 0.23 Performance Management Stage 1+2
// (security fixes, revision workflow). 0.22 clear notifications (delete own, hide team ones). 0.21 notifications to
// custom roles; Performance Management collections (Neo's merge). 0.20 ticket quotes & invoices. 0.19 What's New.
// 0.18 agreement renewals (staff list readable); owner payment status, custom role delete. 0.17 delete fill-in
// links; Roles page. 0.16 booking numbers, Willow booking import, Operations edit bookings, offline payments for
// Operations. 0.15 master files, fill-in links (Neo). 0.14 Agreements. 0.13 utility bills, door passcodes, offline
// payments, unit types. 0.12 page access. 0.10 anonymous complaint notifications. 0.9 New Owner Listings.
// 0.8 profile pictures (avatars). 0.7 month summaries (unitMonths, months.summary).
// 0.6 every role signs in; Portfolio for Operations/Procurement/Marketing; direct bookings. 0.5 offline inquiries,
// tenants, offline bookings, Issues, SOPs, complaints, Playbook, brand logos. 0.4 month-end completion is per unit.
// 0.3 HR manages staff accounts and reads the audit log.
// Merged in: rules_ops.txt, rules_dash.txt, rules_directbooking.txt, rules_hr.txt, rules_portfolio.txt, rules_scale.txt.
// Roles come from users/{uid}.role, set on the Staff accounts page (or tools/set-role.js for the first Director).
// Rules OR together: a request is allowed if any matching allow line allows it.
service cloud.firestore {
  match /databases/{database}/documents {

    // ================= Helpers =================

    // ---- Roles ----
    function signedIn()   { return request.auth != null; }
    // The role is read from the person's staff record. A switched-off record (active == false) has no role.
    function myRecord()   { return /databases/$(database)/documents/users/$(request.auth.uid); }
    function role() {
      return signedIn() && exists(myRecord()) && get(myRecord()).data.get('active', true) == true
        ? get(myRecord()).data.get('role', null) : null;
    }
    function isDirector() { return role() == 'director'; }
    function isIT()       { return role() == 'it'; }
    function isHR()       { return role() == 'hr'; }
    function opsRole()    { return role() == 'operations'; }
    // Any active staff record with a role (every role, including IT).
    function anyStaff()   { return role() != null; }
    // Staff accounts: Director and HR. HR can't create, edit or promote anyone to Director.
    function staffAdmin() { return isDirector() || isHR(); }
    function hrOrDir()    { return isHR() || isDirector(); }

    // ---- Page access (Draft 0.12) ----
    // What each role gets before anyone changes its ticks. KEEP IN STEP WITH PRESETS in lib/access.js.
    function presetFor(r) {
      return {
        'finance': ['reports.view', 'reports.edit', 'ezeeUpload.view', 'ezeeUpload.edit', 'expenses.view', 'expenses.edit',
          'monthEnd.view', 'monthEnd.edit', 'invoices.view', 'invoices.edit', 'offlinePayments.view', 'offlinePayments.edit',
          'portfolio.view', 'portfolio.edit', 'bulkUpload.view', 'bulkUpload.edit', 'offlineInquiries.view', 'offlineInquiries.edit'],
        'operations': ['portfolio.view', 'offlineInquiries.view', 'offlineInquiries.edit', 'bookingForms.view', 'newOwnerListings.view', 'offlinePayments.view'],
        'it': [],
        'hr': ['playbook.edit', 'sops.edit'],
        'procurement': ['portfolio.view', 'newOwnerListings.view', 'newOwnerListings.edit'],
        'marketing': ['portfolio.view', 'newOwnerListings.view', 'newOwnerListings.edit']
      }.get(r, []);
    }
    // Draft 0.17: the Director can change a role's usual pages and make new roles on the Roles page, saved in roles/{id}.
    // A role with a roles/{id} document uses its perms list; the built-in lists above are the fallback.
    function roleDoc(r)     { return /databases/$(database)/documents/roles/$(r); }
    function roleDefault(r) { return exists(roleDoc(r)) ? get(roleDoc(r)).data.get('perms', presetFor(r)) : presetFor(r); }
    // The person's ticks: saved on their record, or their role's usual pages. A switched-off record has none.
    function myPerms()    { return role() != null ? get(myRecord()).data.get('perms', roleDefault(role())) : []; }
    function can(p)       { return isDirector() || p in myPerms(); }

    // Finance data: any Finance page lets them read it; any Finance page ticked for Edit lets them change it.
    function finEdit()    { return isDirector() || myPerms().hasAny(['ezeeUpload.edit', 'expenses.edit', 'monthEnd.edit', 'invoices.edit', 'offlinePayments.edit']); }
    function finView()    { return finEdit() || myPerms().hasAny(['reports.view', 'ezeeUpload.view', 'expenses.view', 'monthEnd.view', 'invoices.view']); }
    function finOrDir()   { return finEdit(); }
    function isFinance()  { return finEdit(); }
    // Finance-data readers, plus IT (view-only on everything, as before).
    function staff()      { return finView() || isIT(); }
    // Offline Inquiries page: works the inquiries assigned to them (Create booking, tenants, direct bookings).
    function isOps()      { return can('offlineInquiries.view'); }
    // Portfolio: View reads owners, properties, units and bookings. Edit (or Bulk Upload Edit) changes them,
    // terms and bank details included.
    function portfolioViewer() { return can('portfolio.view'); }
    function portfolioEditor() { return finEdit() || can('portfolio.edit') || can('bulkUpload.edit'); }
    // Operations and Marketing with Portfolio View may also add properties, units and owners (no terms or bank details).
    function portfolioAdder()  { return role() in ['operations', 'marketing'] && portfolioViewer(); }
    // Marketing with Portfolio View also edit names and details (Khairul 27 Oct).
    function isMkt()      { return role() == 'marketing' && portfolioViewer(); }
    // New Owner Listings.
    function listingViewer()   { return can('newOwnerListings.view'); }
    function listingEditor()   { return can('newOwnerListings.edit'); }

    // ---- Paths and writes ----
    function docPath(col, id)    { return /databases/$(database)/documents/$(col)/$(id); }
    function changed()           { return request.resource.data.diff(resource.data).affectedKeys(); }
    function newKeysOnly(keys)   { return request.resource.data.keys().hasOnly(keys); }
    function createdNow(col, id) { return !exists(docPath(col, id)) && existsAfter(docPath(col, id)); }

    // ---- Month-end: completion is per unit, statements/{unitId}_{month} ----
    function statementPath(unitId, month) {
      return /databases/$(database)/documents/statements/$(unitId + '_' + month);
    }
    function unitCompleted(unitId, month) {
      return (exists(statementPath(unitId, month))
        && get(statementPath(unitId, month)).data.status == 'completed')
        // Finance sent it to the Director: its numbers are frozen until approved, sent back or pulled back.
        || (exists(approvalPath(unitId, month))
        && get(approvalPath(unitId, month)).data.status == 'submitted');
    }
    function approvalPath(unitId, month) {
      return /databases/$(database)/documents/approvals/$(unitId + '_' + month);
    }
    function unitMonthKeys() {
      return ['propertyId', 'month', 'unitId', 'unitCode', 'engineVersion', 'inUnits', 'hasTerms', 'arrangement', 'arrangementType', 'fixedRentAmount',
        'firstBookingId', 'row', 'noUnit', 'dash', 'statement', 'stale', 'dirtyRev', 'cleanRev', 'marks', 'computedAt', 'computedBy'];
    }

    // ---- Operations: inquiries, Create booking, direct bookings ----
    function assignedToMe(inqId) { return get(docPath('offlineInquiries', inqId)).data.get('assignedToUid', null) == request.auth.uid; }
    // True only inside the Create booking transaction: offline_{id} doesn't exist before and does after.
    function bookingMadeNow(inqId) {
      return !exists(docPath('offlineBookings', 'offline_' + inqId)) && existsAfter(docPath('offlineBookings', 'offline_' + inqId));
    }
    // Operations write a tenant only through Create booking on an inquiry assigned to them, and only the tenant it points at.
    function opsBooking(inqId, tenantId) {
      return isOps() && inqId is string && assignedToMe(inqId) && bookingMadeNow(inqId)
        && getAfter(docPath('offlineBookings', 'offline_' + inqId)).data.tenantId == tenantId
        && getAfter(docPath('offlineInquiries', inqId)).data.tenantId == tenantId;
    }
    // True only inside the transaction that creates this direct booking (offline_BK-0001) for this tenant.
    function directBookingMadeNow(bookingId, tenantId) {
      return bookingId is string && bookingId.matches('offline_BK-[0-9]+')
        && !exists(docPath('offlineBookings', bookingId))
        && getAfter(docPath('offlineBookings', bookingId)).data.tenantId == tenantId
        && getAfter(docPath('offlineBookings', bookingId)).data.createdBy == request.auth.uid;
    }

    // ---- Issues: the tag each role answers to ('Admin' has no sign-in role yet) ----
    function myIssueTag() {
      return { 'finance': 'Finance', 'it': 'IT', 'hr': 'HR', 'operations': 'Operations', 'procurement': 'Procurement', 'marketing': 'Marketing' }
        .get(role(), exists(roleDoc(role())) ? get(roleDoc(role())).data.get('name', '-') : '-');   // a role made on the Roles page is tagged by its name
    }
    function canSeeIssue(d) { return anyStaff() && (isDirector() || myIssueTag() in d.tags || d.raisedByUid == request.auth.uid); }

    // ---- Complaints ----
    function complaintAfter(id) { return getAfter(docPath('complaints', id)).data; }
    function complaintNow(id)   { return get(docPath('complaints', id)).data; }
    // Draft 0.38: a Director complaint is between the Directors and the HR person who sent it (fromId), not all of HR
    // Draft 0.40: reads the complaint and the role once each (fewer get() calls; Firestore caps them per request)
    function dirSide(id) {
      let c = complaintNow(id);
      let r = role();
      return c.kind == 'director' && (r == 'director' || (r == 'hr' && c.get('fromId', null) == request.auth.uid));
    }

    // ================= Shared: private data, accounts, counters, logs =================

    // Personal data lives only in {doc}/private/main. IT never reads it. Complaint text (HR/Directors), new owner
    // listings' contact details (Director/Procurement) and COH marks (evaluator + HR/Director, Draft 0.32) have
    // their own rules below.
    match /{parent=**}/private/{docId} {
      allow read, write: if finOrDir() && parent[0] != 'complaints' && parent[0] != 'newOwnerListings'
        && parent[0] != 'cohEvaluations';
      // Returning tenant search: collectionGroup('private') where kind == 'tenant'. kind is written only on
      // tenants/{id}/private/main; Operations can't add it to an inquiry's private doc.
      allow read: if (isOps() || finOrDir()) && resource.data.get('kind', '') == 'tenant';
    }

    match /users/{uid} {
      // Page ticks, when saved, are a list.
      function permsOk() { return !('perms' in request.resource.data) || request.resource.data.perms is list; }
      allow read: if signedIn() && (request.auth.uid == uid || staffAdmin() || isIT());
      // Agreement renewals: everyone picks who is in charge of an agreement from the staff list.
      allow read: if anyStaff();
      allow create: if permsOk() && (isDirector() || (isHR() && request.resource.data.role != 'director'));
      // A Director cannot remove their own Director role or switch themselves off (no lock-out).
      allow update: if isDirector() && permsOk() && (uid != request.auth.uid
        || (request.resource.data.role == 'director' && request.resource.data.get('active', true) == true));
      // HR: anyone except Directors and themselves, and never to Director.
      allow update: if isHR() && permsOk() && uid != request.auth.uid
        && resource.data.role != 'director' && request.resource.data.role != 'director';
      // Sign-in stamps lastLoginAt on your own record (Team activity).
      allow update: if signedIn() && request.auth.uid == uid && changed().hasOnly(['lastLoginAt']);
      allow delete: if false;
    }

    // Roles page (Director only). Everyone signed in reads, so the app can show names and usual pages after sign-in.
    match /roles/{rid} {
      allow read: if signedIn();
      allow create, update: if isDirector() && request.resource.data.perms is list && rid != 'director';
      allow delete: if isDirector() && rid != 'director';
    }

    match /config/{docId} {
      allow read: if staff();
      allow write: if isDirector();
    }

    // Unit types added with "+ Add type" on Add unit: anyone who can add or edit units may add to the list.
    match /config/unitTypes {
      allow write: if (portfolioEditor() || portfolioAdder() || isMkt())
        && request.resource.data.keys().hasOnly(['list']) && request.resource.data.list is list && request.resource.data.list.size() < 100;
    }

    // Numbered IDs (LD-, TEN-, IS-, BK-, CP-, DC-, NL-): taken one at a time inside a transaction.
    match /counters/{name} {
      allow read: if (name == 'offlineInquiries' && finOrDir())
        || (name == 'tenants' && (finOrDir() || isOps()))
        || (name == 'issues' && anyStaff());
      allow create: if request.resource.data.next == 2 && (
           (name == 'offlineInquiries' && isDirector())
        || (name == 'tenants' && (finOrDir() || isOps()))
        || (name == 'issues' && anyStaff()));
      allow update: if request.resource.data.next == resource.data.next + 1 && (
           (name == 'offlineInquiries' && isDirector())
        || (name == 'tenants' && (finOrDir() || isOps()))
        || (name == 'issues' && anyStaff()));
      // Direct bookings.
      allow read: if name == 'offlineBookings' && (finOrDir() || isOps());
      allow create: if name == 'offlineBookings' && (finOrDir() || isOps()) && request.resource.data.next == 2;
      allow update: if name == 'offlineBookings' && (finOrDir() || isOps()) && request.resource.data.next == resource.data.next + 1;
      // Complaints.
      allow read: if name == 'staffComplaints' && anyStaff();
      allow read: if name == 'directorComplaints' && hrOrDir();
      allow create: if ((name == 'staffComplaints' && anyStaff()) || (name == 'directorComplaints' && hrOrDir()))
        && request.resource.data.next == 2;
      allow update: if ((name == 'staffComplaints' && anyStaff()) || (name == 'directorComplaints' && hrOrDir()))
        && request.resource.data.next == resource.data.next + 1;
      // Salary advances (Draft 0.42).
      allow read: if name == 'advances' && anyStaff();
      allow create: if name == 'advances' && anyStaff() && request.resource.data.next == 2;
      allow update: if name == 'advances' && anyStaff() && request.resource.data.next == resource.data.next + 1;
      // New owner listings.
      allow read: if name == 'newOwnerListings' && listingEditor();
      allow create: if name == 'newOwnerListings' && listingEditor() && request.resource.data.next == 2;
      allow update: if name == 'newOwnerListings' && listingEditor() && request.resource.data.next == resource.data.next + 1;
      allow delete: if false;
    }

    // What's New: every staff member reads the updates; only a Director posts, edits or deletes them.
    match /updates/{id} {
      allow read: if anyStaff();
      allow create, update, delete: if isDirector();
    }

    // HR Announcements (Draft 0.37, 5 Nov 2026). Posted by HR and Directors to Everyone or chosen roles (role ids).
    match /announcements/{id} {
      function annPoster() { return isHR() || isDirector(); }
      function annOk() {
        return request.resource.data.title is string && request.resource.data.title.size() > 0 && request.resource.data.title.size() <= 150
          && request.resource.data.message is string && request.resource.data.message.size() > 0 && request.resource.data.message.size() <= 5000
          && request.resource.data.audience is list && request.resource.data.audience.size() > 0 && request.resource.data.audience.size() <= 40
          && request.resource.data.get('pinned', false) is bool
          && request.resource.data.get('files', []) is list && request.resource.data.get('files', []).size() <= 10;
      }
      allow read: if annPoster() || (anyStaff() && resource.data.audience.hasAny([role(), 'everyone']));
      allow create: if annPoster() && annOk() && request.resource.data.createdBy == request.auth.uid;
      allow update: if annPoster() && annOk() && request.resource.data.createdBy == resource.data.createdBy
        && request.resource.data.createdAt == resource.data.createdAt;
      allow delete: if annPoster();

      // Opened: once per person (no update), only for an announcement meant for them
      match /views/{uid} {
        function annForMe() {
          return get(/databases/$(database)/documents/announcements/$(id)).data.audience.hasAny([role(), 'everyone']);
        }
        allow read: if signedIn() && (request.auth.uid == uid || isHR() || isDirector());
        allow create: if anyStaff() && request.auth.uid == uid && annForMe()
          && request.resource.data.keys().hasOnly(['viewedAt', 'name', 'role'])
          && request.resource.data.viewedAt == request.time;
        allow delete: if isHR() || isDirector();
      }
    }
    // Each person's own list of announcements they have opened (dashboard banner, Unread filter)
    match /announcementReads/{uid} {
      allow read: if signedIn() && request.auth.uid == uid;
      allow create, update: if anyStaff() && request.auth.uid == uid
        && request.resource.data.keys().hasOnly(['ids']) && request.resource.data.ids is map;
    }

    // Every role writes its own audit entries; an anonymous complaint is logged with NO uid.
    match /auditLog/{id} {
      allow read: if staff() || isHR();
      allow create: if anyStaff() && request.resource.data.uid == request.auth.uid;
      allow create: if anyStaff() && request.resource.data.uid == null && request.resource.data.userName == 'Anonymous'
        && request.resource.data.role == null && request.resource.data.action == 'complaint.create';
      allow update, delete: if false;
    }

    match /accessLog/{id} {
      allow read: if isDirector() || isIT();
      allow create: if isIT() && request.resource.data.uid == request.auth.uid;
      allow update, delete: if false;
    }

    // Appearance: userPrefs/{uid} = { brand, mode, custom, updatedAt }. Each person reads and writes only their own.
    match /userPrefs/{uid} {
      allow read, create, update: if anyStaff() && request.auth.uid == uid;
      allow delete: if false;
    }

    // Profile pictures: avatars/{uid} = { src, updatedAt }, a 128 px square data URL. Each person writes only their own.
    match /avatars/{uid} {
      allow read: if anyStaff();
      allow create, update: if anyStaff() && request.auth.uid == uid
        && newKeysOnly(['src', 'updatedAt'])
        && request.resource.data.src is string && request.resource.data.src.size() <= 60000
        && request.resource.data.src.matches('^data:image/(webp|jpeg|png);base64,.*')
        && request.resource.data.updatedAt == request.time;
      allow delete: if anyStaff() && request.auth.uid == uid;
    }

    // Brand logos: brandLogos/light and brandLogos/dark, a data URL each (<= 512 px). Director edits.
    match /brandLogos/{key} {
      allow read: if anyStaff();
      allow create, update: if isDirector() && key in ['light', 'dark']
        && request.resource.data.src is string && request.resource.data.src.size() <= 280000
        && request.resource.data.src.matches('^data:image/(png|webp);base64,.*');
      allow delete: if false;
    }

    // ================= Setup data (Portfolio) =================
    // Finance/Directors write. Operations, Procurement and Marketing read the parents only (no terms, rates or
    // owners' private data). Operations and Marketing may also create properties, units and owners (create only, never edit).
    // Version documents are add-only: a change is a new document.

    match /properties/{propertyId} {
      allow read: if staff() || portfolioViewer();
      allow write: if portfolioEditor();
      allow create: if portfolioAdder() && newKeysOnly(['name', 'code', 'info', 'active', 'createdAt', 'createdBy'])
        && request.resource.data.active == true && request.resource.data.createdBy == request.auth.uid
        && request.resource.data.name is string && request.resource.data.code is string
        && (!('info' in request.resource.data) || request.resource.data.info.keys().hasOnly(['address', 'city', 'state', 'ezeeAccount', 'ezeeName']));
      // The batch that adds a unit notes it on its property (summaryMarks); the only change Operations may make.
      allow update: if portfolioAdder() && changed().hasOnly(['summaryMarks']);
      // Marketing also edit the name and details (Khairul 27 Oct); never the short code or anything money.
      allow update: if isMkt() && changed().hasOnly(['name', 'info', 'updatedAt', 'updatedBy', 'summaryMarks'])
        && request.resource.data.info.keys().hasOnly(['address', 'city', 'state', 'ezeeAccount', 'ezeeName']);
      match /rateVersions/{v} {
        allow read: if staff() || portfolioEditor();
        allow create: if portfolioEditor() && request.resource.data.reason is string;
        // Operations: only the default OTA rates, only in the batch that creates the property.
        allow create: if portfolioAdder() && v == '2000-01_default' && createdNow('properties', propertyId)
          && request.resource.data.effectiveFrom == '2000-01' && request.resource.data.createdBy == request.auth.uid
          && newKeysOnly(['effectiveFrom', 'ota', 'earlyCheckInToOwner', 'tourismTaxPerNight', 'reason', 'createdBy', 'createdByName', 'createdAt']);
        allow update, delete: if false;
      }
    }

    match /units/{unitId} {
      allow read: if staff() || portfolioViewer();
      allow create, update: if portfolioEditor();
      allow delete: if isDirector();   // safe delete: the page only offers it for units with no history
      // Operations: no terms (arrangement, fixed rent, fees).
      allow create: if portfolioAdder() && newKeysOnly(['propertyId', 'unitCode', 'ezeeRoomMatch', 'aliases', 'ownerId', 'info', 'active',
          'createdAt', 'createdBy', 'updatedAt', 'updatedBy'])
        && request.resource.data.active == true && request.resource.data.createdBy == request.auth.uid
        && exists(docPath('properties', request.resource.data.propertyId))
        && request.resource.data.info.keys().hasOnly(['type', 'bedrooms', 'bathrooms', 'sizeSqft', 'carParks', 'tnb', 'water', 'wifi', 'sewerage', 'jmb']);
      // Marketing edit unit details and eZee names; not the owner link, status or terms.
      allow update: if isMkt() && changed().hasOnly(['aliases', 'info', 'updatedAt', 'updatedBy'])
        && request.resource.data.info.keys().hasOnly(['type', 'bedrooms', 'bathrooms', 'sizeSqft', 'carParks', 'tnb', 'water', 'wifi', 'sewerage', 'jmb']);
      match /terms/{v} {
        allow read: if staff() || portfolioEditor();
        allow create: if portfolioEditor() && request.resource.data.reason is string;
        allow update: if false;
        allow delete: if isDirector();   // only when a unit is safe-deleted
      }
      match /ownership/{id} {
        allow read: if staff() || portfolioEditor();
        allow write: if portfolioEditor();
      }
    }

    // The owner parent holds bankLast4 (not shown to portfolio viewers); Operations create it with none.
    match /owners/{ownerId} {
      allow read: if staff() || portfolioViewer();
      allow create, update: if portfolioEditor();
      allow delete: if isDirector();   // safe delete: the page only offers it for owners with no units
      allow create: if portfolioAdder() && newKeysOnly(['code', 'active', 'bankLast4', 'createdAt', 'createdBy', 'updatedAt', 'updatedBy'])
        && request.resource.data.active == true && request.resource.data.get('bankLast4', null) == null
        && request.resource.data.createdBy == request.auth.uid;
      allow update: if isMkt() && changed().hasOnly(['updatedAt', 'updatedBy']);
      // Operations write name and contact details once, in the batch that creates the owner, and never read them back.
      match /private/{docId} {
        // Portfolio Edit: names, contact and bank details.
        allow read, write: if portfolioEditor() && docId == 'main';
        allow create: if portfolioAdder() && docId == 'main' && createdNow('owners', ownerId)
          && newKeysOnly(['fullName', 'ic', 'email', 'phone', 'dob', 'whatsapp', 'wechat', 'address', 'coOwners', 'updatedAt', 'updatedBy'])
          && request.resource.data.updatedBy == request.auth.uid;
        // Marketing read and edit names and contact details (Khairul 27 Oct). Bank fields share this document: the
        // page hides them and Marketing can't change them.
        allow read: if isMkt() && docId == 'main';
        allow update: if isMkt() && docId == 'main' && request.resource.data.updatedBy == request.auth.uid
          && changed().hasOnly(['fullName', 'ic', 'email', 'phone', 'dob', 'whatsapp', 'wechat', 'address', 'coOwners', 'updatedAt', 'updatedBy']);
      }
    }

    match /agreements/{id} {
      allow read: if staff() || portfolioEditor();
      allow write: if portfolioEditor();
    }

    // ================= Finance: bookings and month-end =================

    // eZee uploads. Operations read the latest for "Last eZee upload" on their dashboard.
    match /importBatches/{id} {
      allow read: if staff() || isOps() || opsRole();
      allow create: if finOrDir();
      allow update, delete: if false;
    }

    // Locked months are protected by the app posting changes as adjustments (CSV-13); Edit on a completed month goes
    // through a Director Override revision.
    // ===== Role dashboards (dash): Operations read today's check-ins/outs (parent docs only, no write).
    match /bookings/{reservationNo} {
      allow read: if staff() || isOps() || opsRole();
      allow create, update: if finOrDir();
      // Draft 0.24 (Khairul): only a booking already removed by hand on Month-end (cancelled + removedByHand), by Finance/Director
      allow delete: if finOrDir() && resource.data.status == 'cancelled' && resource.data.get('removedByHand', null) != null;
    }

    // Each unit's payout per month: completed statements, and Finance's past statements uploaded as reference.
    match /payoutHistory/{id} {
      allow read: if staff();
      allow create, update: if finOrDir();
      allow delete: if isDirector();
    }

    // months/{propertyId}_{month}: open -> partial -> completed as units are completed, plus a `summary` field.
    match /months/{id} {
      allow read: if staff();
      allow create: if finOrDir() && request.resource.data.status in ['open', 'partial', 'completed'];
      // Once completed, only a Director may change the status (Override / unit reopen).
      allow update: if finOrDir() && (resource.data.status != 'completed' || isDirector())
        && request.resource.data.status in ['open', 'partial', 'completed'];
      // Summary-only writes, on any month.
      allow create: if finOrDir()
        && newKeysOnly(['propertyId', 'month', 'summary'])
        && id == request.resource.data.propertyId + '_' + request.resource.data.month;
      // Pool Sharing check (Draft 0.46): "Confirmed 0 bookings" per unit, with who and when (poolZero only).
      allow create: if finOrDir() && newKeysOnly(['propertyId', 'month', 'poolZero'])
        && id == request.resource.data.propertyId + '_' + request.resource.data.month;
      allow update: if finOrDir() && changed().hasOnly(['poolZero']);
      allow update: if finOrDir()
        && changed().hasOnly(['propertyId', 'month', 'summary'])
        && request.resource.data.propertyId == resource.data.get('propertyId', request.resource.data.propertyId)
        && request.resource.data.month == resource.data.get('month', request.resource.data.month);
      // Approve & complete on a summary-only month document (no status yet means open).
      allow update: if finOrDir() && resource.data.get('status', 'open') != 'completed'
        && request.resource.data.status in ['open', 'partial', 'completed'];
      allow delete: if false;
    }

    // ===== Month summaries (scale): unitMonths/{unitId}_{month}, worked out once by lib/summaries.js. Never deleted.
    match /unitMonths/{id} {
      allow read: if staff();
      allow create, update: if finOrDir()
        && request.resource.data.keys().hasOnly(unitMonthKeys())
        && request.resource.data.propertyId is string && request.resource.data.month is string && request.resource.data.unitId is string
        && id == request.resource.data.unitId + '_' + request.resource.data.month;
      allow delete: if false;
    }

    match /expenses/{id} {
      allow read: if staff();
      allow create: if finOrDir()
        && !unitCompleted(request.resource.data.unitId, request.resource.data.month);
      // Automatic Brought Forward lines are only rewritten by Approve & complete / Reopen (auto stays true).
      allow update: if finOrDir()
        && (resource.data.auto != true || request.resource.data.auto == true)
        && !unitCompleted(resource.data.unitId, resource.data.month)
        && !unitCompleted(request.resource.data.unitId, request.resource.data.month)
        && request.resource.data.month == resource.data.month;
      allow delete: if false;   // "Remove" sets deleted = true
    }

    match /statements/{id} {
      allow read: if staff();
      // Approve & complete, one unit at a time. Only a Director completes (Finance sends to the Director: approvals below).
      allow create: if isDirector() && request.resource.data.revision == 1 && request.resource.data.status == 'completed';
      // Director reopens one unit: same revision, status 'reopened', and the revision is saved first.
      allow update: if isDirector()
        && resource.data.status == 'completed' && request.resource.data.status == 'reopened'
        && resource.data.get('paymentStatus', '') != 'paid'
        && request.resource.data.revision == resource.data.revision
        && exists(/databases/$(database)/documents/statements/$(id)/revisions/$(string(resource.data.revision)));
      // Director Override (completing a reopened unit again): revision goes up by one, the old one saved first.
      allow update: if isDirector()
        && request.resource.data.status == 'completed'
        && request.resource.data.revision == resource.data.revision + 1
        && exists(/databases/$(database)/documents/statements/$(id)/revisions/$(string(resource.data.revision)));
      // Owner payment (Draft 0.18, Invoices & Receipts): Finance or a Director marks a completed statement Paid (pay slip in Drive);
      // only a Director sets it back to pending (Undo payment). Nothing else on the statement changes.
      allow update: if (isDirector() || isFinance())
        && resource.data.status == 'completed' && request.resource.data.status == 'completed'
        && request.resource.data.revision == resource.data.revision
        && request.resource.data.diff(resource.data).affectedKeys().hasOnly(['paymentStatus', 'paidDate', 'paidAmount', 'paidRef', 'paidBy', 'paidByName', 'paidAt', 'payUndoReason', 'payUndoBy', 'payUndoByName', 'payUndoAt'])
        && (request.resource.data.paymentStatus == 'paid' || (isDirector() && request.resource.data.paymentStatus == 'pending'));
      allow delete: if false;
      match /revisions/{rev} {
        allow read: if staff();
        allow create: if isDirector();
        allow update, delete: if false;
      }
    }

    // Finance sends a unit's statement to the Director (Statement Approvals page). id = unitId_month, same as statements.
    // submitted -> approved (Director completes it, same batch as the statement) or returned (Director, reason) or
    // withdrawn (Finance pulls it back, reason). Returned / withdrawn can be sent again. After a Director reopen, an approved
    // one can be sent again too.
    match /approvals/{id} {
      allow read: if staff();
      allow create: if finOrDir() && request.resource.data.status == 'submitted'
        && id == request.resource.data.unitId + '_' + request.resource.data.month
        && request.resource.data.submittedBy == request.auth.uid
        && (!exists(statementPath(request.resource.data.unitId, request.resource.data.month))
          || get(statementPath(request.resource.data.unitId, request.resource.data.month)).data.status == 'reopened');
      allow update: if finOrDir() && request.resource.data.status == 'submitted' && request.resource.data.submittedBy == request.auth.uid
        && (resource.data.status in ['returned', 'withdrawn']
          || (resource.data.status == 'approved' && get(statementPath(resource.data.unitId, resource.data.month)).data.status == 'reopened'));
      allow update: if finOrDir() && resource.data.status == 'submitted' && request.resource.data.status == 'withdrawn'
        && request.resource.data.withdrawReason is string && request.resource.data.withdrawReason.size() > 0;
      allow update: if isDirector() && resource.data.status == 'submitted'
        && (request.resource.data.status == 'approved'
          || (request.resource.data.status == 'returned' && request.resource.data.returnReason is string && request.resource.data.returnReason.size() > 0));
      allow delete: if false;
    }

    match /exports/{id} {
      allow read: if staff();
      allow create: if finOrDir() || can('reports.edit');
      allow update, delete: if false;
    }

    // ================= Operations: inquiries, tenants, offline bookings, Issues =================

    // Directors log inquiries; Finance and Directors read all; IT reads the parent only (no contact details);
    // Operations read and update only the ones assigned to them.
    match /offlineInquiries/{id} {
      allow read: if finOrDir() || isIT() || (isOps() && resource.data.assignedToUid == request.auth.uid);
      allow create: if isDirector()
        && request.resource.data.loggedByUid == request.auth.uid
        && request.resource.data.status in ['new', 'interested', 'considering', 'uninterested']
        && request.resource.data.get('bookingId', null) == null;
      // Directors: anything, including (re)assigning.
      allow update: if isDirector() && request.resource.data.status in ['new', 'interested', 'considering', 'uninterested', 'booked'];
      // Finance: status, notes, booking; not the assignee.
      allow update: if isFinance()
        && !changed().hasAny(['assignedToUid', 'assignedToName', 'loggedByUid', 'loggedByName', 'createdAt'])
        && request.resource.data.status in ['new', 'interested', 'considering', 'uninterested', 'booked'];
      // The assignee: status, history and (only in Create booking) the tenant and booking links.
      allow update: if isOps() && resource.data.assignedToUid == request.auth.uid
        && changed().hasOnly(['status', 'history', 'updatedAt', 'tenantId', 'bookingId'])
        && request.resource.data.status in ['new', 'interested', 'considering', 'uninterested', 'booked']
        && (bookingMadeNow(id)
            || (!changed().hasAny(['tenantId', 'bookingId']) && (request.resource.data.status != 'booked' || resource.data.status == 'booked')));
      allow delete: if false;
      // Contact details: Finance/Directors through the catch-all; the assignee here.
      match /private/{docId} {
        allow read: if isOps() && assignedToMe(id);
        allow create, update: if isOps() && assignedToMe(id)
          && newKeysOnly(['contactName', 'phone', 'phoneKey', 'email']);
        allow delete: if false;
      }
    }

    // Written by Finance/Directors, and by Operations only inside Create booking (opsBooking, lastInquiryId)
    // or a direct booking (directBookingMadeNow, lastBookingId).
    match /tenants/{tenantId} {
      allow read: if finOrDir() || isOps();
      allow create, update: if finOrDir();
      allow create, update: if opsBooking(request.resource.data.get('lastInquiryId', null), tenantId)
        && (resource == null || changed().hasOnly(['status', 'lastInquiryId', 'updatedAt', 'updatedBy']));
      allow create, update: if isOps() && directBookingMadeNow(request.resource.data.get('lastBookingId', null), tenantId)
        && (resource == null || changed().hasOnly(['status', 'lastBookingId', 'updatedAt', 'updatedBy']));
      allow delete: if false;
      match /private/{docId} {
        allow read: if isOps();
        allow create, update: if opsBooking(getAfter(docPath('tenants', tenantId)).data.get('lastInquiryId', null), tenantId);
        allow create, update: if isOps()
          && directBookingMadeNow(getAfter(docPath('tenants', tenantId)).data.get('lastBookingId', null), tenantId);
        allow delete: if false;
      }
    }

    // Offline payments (Finance > Offline Payments): submitted and checked by Finance/Director.
    // View and Edit are separate ticks: Offline Payments View reads; Offline Payments Edit creates and changes.
    match /offlinePayments/{id} {
      allow read: if can('offlinePayments.view') || can('offlinePayments.edit');
      allow create: if can('offlinePayments.edit') && request.resource.data.createdBy == request.auth.uid && request.resource.data.status in ['Pending', 'Checked', 'Unknown'];
      allow update: if can('offlinePayments.edit');
      // The Booking Form saves the booking's payment here (Pending), in the same write as the booking itself.
      allow create: if (isOps() || finOrDir()) && request.resource.data.createdBy == request.auth.uid && request.resource.data.status == 'Pending'
        && request.resource.data.bookingId is string && !exists(docPath('offlineBookings', request.resource.data.bookingId))
        && existsAfter(docPath('offlineBookings', request.resource.data.bookingId));
      // Operations fill in a payment that has no receipt (status Unknown): saving it makes it Edited, and Finance is told.
      allow update: if role() == 'operations' && can('offlinePayments.view') && resource.data.status == 'Unknown' && request.resource.data.status == 'Edited'
        && !changed().hasAny(['createdBy', 'createdAt', 'submittedByName', 'verifiedByName', 'verifiedDate', 'remarks']);
      allow delete: if false;
    }
    // Utility bills logged against an offline booking (Operations > Booking Forms > Utility Lodgment Form); one per booking.
    match /utilityBills/{bookingId} {
      // Booking Forms View is the only tick that page has, so it gives the form (read, save and update a bill).
      allow read: if finOrDir() || isOps() || can('bookingForms.view');
      allow create: if (finOrDir() || isOps() || can('bookingForms.view')) && request.resource.data.createdBy == request.auth.uid
        && exists(docPath('offlineBookings', bookingId));
      allow update: if finOrDir() || can('bookingForms.view');
      // Draft 0.36: removed with its booking, only while the booking is cancelled.
      allow delete: if (finOrDir() || isOps()) && get(docPath('offlineBookings', bookingId)).data.get('status', '') == 'cancelled';
    }

    // Not the bookings collection: Finance's month-end reads bookings, and these are paid from eZee.
    // offline_{inquiryId} from Create booking, or offline_BK-0001 for a direct booking (no inquiry).
    match /offlineBookings/{bookingId} {
      allow read: if finOrDir() || isOps() || portfolioViewer();
      allow create: if finOrDir() && bookingId == 'offline_' + request.resource.data.inquiryId;
      allow update: if finOrDir() && request.resource.data.inquiryId == resource.data.inquiryId;
      // Operations: Create booking on their own inquiry (the inquiry must point back and be booked in the same write).
      allow create: if isOps() && bookingId == 'offline_' + request.resource.data.inquiryId
        && assignedToMe(request.resource.data.inquiryId)
        && getAfter(docPath('offlineInquiries', request.resource.data.inquiryId)).data.bookingId == bookingId
        && getAfter(docPath('offlineInquiries', request.resource.data.inquiryId)).data.status == 'booked';
      // ...and adding the eZee reservation no. later.
      allow update: if isOps() && assignedToMe(resource.data.inquiryId)
        && changed().hasOnly(['ezeeReservationNo', 'updatedAt', 'updatedBy']);
      // Operations edit any booking's details (Portfolio > Bookings > open a booking); who, source and the inquiry link stay as they were.
      allow update: if isOps() && !changed().hasAny(['createdBy', 'createdAt', 'source', 'inquiryId', 'bookingNo', 'tenantId', 'propertyId', 'unitId']);
      // Direct booking (Portfolio > Bookings > + New booking).
      allow create: if (finOrDir() || isOps()) && bookingId.matches('offline_BK-[0-9]+')
        && request.resource.data.source == 'direct' && request.resource.data.inquiryId == null
        && request.resource.data.createdBy == request.auth.uid
        && request.resource.data.tenantId is string
        && getAfter(docPath('tenants', request.resource.data.tenantId)) != null;
      // Willow Booking Details bulk upload (Portfolio > Bulk Upload): Finance or a Director, offline_{booking no.} such as offline_DM-014.
      allow create: if finOrDir() && bookingId.matches('offline_[A-Z0-9]+-[0-9]+') && request.resource.data.source == 'import'
        && request.resource.data.createdBy == request.auth.uid;
      // Draft 0.36: delete for good, only a cancelled booking (the page also checks no payment is recorded).
      allow delete: if (finOrDir() || isOps()) && resource.data.get('status', '') == 'cancelled';
      // Door passcodes for the booking (Booking Form).
      match /private/{doc} {
        allow read: if finOrDir() || isOps();
        allow create: if (finOrDir() || isOps()) && existsAfter(docPath('offlineBookings', bookingId));
        allow update: if finOrDir() || isOps();
        allow delete: if (finOrDir() || isOps()) && get(docPath('offlineBookings', bookingId)).data.get('status', '') == 'cancelled';
      }
    }

    // Issues: seen by the tagged roles, the person who raised it and Directors. Every role raises tickets.
    // Completed tickets are locked.
    match /issues/{id} {
      allow read: if canSeeIssue(resource.data);
      allow create: if anyStaff()
        && request.resource.data.raisedByUid == request.auth.uid
        && request.resource.data.status == 'open'
        && request.resource.data.tags is list && request.resource.data.tags.size() > 0;
      // A comment (anyone who can see it): counters, last poster and the ticket's audit trail.
      allow update: if anyStaff() && canSeeIssue(resource.data) && resource.data.status in ['open', 'progress']
        && changed().hasOnly(['replyCount', 'linkCount', 'lastBy', 'audit', 'updatedAt']);
      // In progress, tags and Mark completed: Directors and the tagged roles.
      allow update: if anyStaff() && resource.data.status in ['open', 'progress']
        && (isDirector() || myIssueTag() in resource.data.tags)
        && changed().hasOnly(['status', 'tags', 'type', 'doneAt', 'doneBy', 'doneByUid', 'audit', 'updatedAt'])
        && (!('type' in request.resource.data) || request.resource.data.type in ['customer', 'inhouse'])
        && request.resource.data.status in ['open', 'progress', 'done']
        && request.resource.data.tags is list && request.resource.data.tags.size() > 0;
      // Draft 0.47: title, description, property and the task system column (tmsStatus), from the Issues page or the task system (TMS),
      // with or without a status change: Directors and the tagged roles, while the ticket is Open or In progress.
      allow update: if anyStaff() && resource.data.status in ['open', 'progress']
        && (isDirector() || myIssueTag() in resource.data.tags)
        && changed().hasOnly(['status', 'doneAt', 'doneBy', 'doneByUid', 'title', 'body', 'property', 'propertyId', 'tmsStatus', 'audit', 'updatedAt'])
        && request.resource.data.status in ['open', 'progress', 'done']
        && (request.resource.data.status != 'done' || request.resource.data.get('doneByUid', '') == request.auth.uid)
        && request.resource.data.get('title', '') is string
        && request.resource.data.get('title', '').size() > 0 && request.resource.data.get('title', '').size() <= 200
        && request.resource.data.get('body', '') is string && request.resource.data.get('body', '').size() <= 5000
        && request.resource.data.get('property', '') is string && request.resource.data.get('property', '').size() <= 80
        && (!('tmsStatus' in request.resource.data) || request.resource.data.tmsStatus is map);
      // Delete ticket: Directors only, any status. Marked deleted with a reason, never removed; nothing changes it after.
      allow update: if isDirector() && resource.data.status != 'deleted'
        && changed().hasOnly(['status', 'deletedAt', 'deletedBy', 'deletedByUid', 'deleteReason', 'audit', 'updatedAt'])
        && request.resource.data.status == 'deleted'
        && request.resource.data.deleteReason is string && request.resource.data.deleteReason.size() > 0;
      allow delete: if false;
      match /replies/{replyId} {
        allow read: if canSeeIssue(get(docPath('issues', id)).data);
        allow create: if anyStaff() && request.resource.data.byUid == request.auth.uid
          && canSeeIssue(get(docPath('issues', id)).data)
          && get(docPath('issues', id)).data.status in ['open', 'progress'];
        allow update, delete: if false;
      }
    }

    // Draft 0.20: quote and invoice for a ticket. Anyone who can see the ticket reads the quote and adds or edits it while
    // it is Quoted or Rejected (it goes back to Quoted). Director and people with the Expenses Edit tick (Finance) approve,
    // reject, add the invoice (which also writes an expense line, expenses rules above) and mark it paid.
    // Always charged to the unit's owner. Nothing changes once the vendor is Paid.
    match /issueQuotes/{id} {
      function priceAccess() { return isDirector() || can('expenses.edit'); }
      function ticketOk() {
        return exists(docPath('issues', id)) && get(docPath('issues', id)).data.status != 'deleted'
          && canSeeIssue(get(docPath('issues', id)).data);
      }
      function quoteKeys() {
        return ['issueId', 'propertyId', 'unitId', 'unitCode', 'chargeTo', 'vendor', 'items', 'total', 'notes', 'status', 'rejectReason',
          'createdAt', 'createdBy', 'createdByName', 'history', 'updatedAt', 'updatedBy'];
      }
      function quoteOk() {
        return request.resource.data.issueId == id && request.resource.data.chargeTo == 'owner'
          && request.resource.data.items is list && request.resource.data.items.size() > 0 && request.resource.data.items.size() <= 20;
      }
      allow read: if anyStaff() && ticketOk();
      // Any staff member: add a quote, or edit one that is Quoted or Rejected. It is saved as Quoted.
      allow create: if anyStaff() && ticketOk() && quoteOk()
        && request.resource.data.status == 'quoted' && request.resource.data.keys().hasOnly(quoteKeys());
      allow update: if anyStaff() && ticketOk() && quoteOk()
        && resource.data.status in ['quoted', 'rejected'] && request.resource.data.status == 'quoted'
        && changed().hasOnly(quoteKeys());
      // Director and Finance: every step.
      allow create, update: if priceAccess() && ticketOk() && quoteOk()
        && request.resource.data.status in ['quoted', 'approved', 'invoiced', 'paid', 'rejected']
        && (resource == null || resource.data.status != 'paid');
      allow delete: if false;
    }

    // Draft 0.24 (Khairul): push notifications. One document per device (the id is the Firebase Cloud Messaging token), holding
    // the uid of the person signed in there. A browser that someone else signs into is taken over by them (same device).
    // Only that person reads or removes it; api/push.js reads them with the service account to send pushes.
    match /pushTokens/{token} {
      allow read, delete: if anyStaff() && resource.data.uid == request.auth.uid;
      allow create, update: if anyStaff() && request.resource.data.uid == request.auth.uid
        && request.resource.data.keys().hasOnly(['uid', 'role', 'device', 'updatedAt']);
    }

    // Notifications: one document per recipient target. recipientUid = one person; recipientRole = everyone in
    // that role (read state is per person in readBy). Both keys are always written, the unused one as null.
    // Anyone signed in with a role may send one, but only as themselves and only with an in-app link.
    // ONE exception (Draft 0.10): an anonymous complaint alert has no sender (createdByUid null, createdByName ''),
    // and may only go to HR with type 'complaint', so the sender of an anonymous complaint cannot be traced from it.
    // Stronger protection against spoofing needs a Cloud Function that sends them.
    match /notifications/{id} {
      function onlyMine(before, after) {
        return after is list
          && after.toSet().difference(before.toSet()).hasOnly([request.auth.uid])
          && before.toSet().difference(after.toSet()).hasOnly([request.auth.uid]);
      }
      allow read: if anyStaff() && (resource.data.recipientUid == request.auth.uid || resource.data.recipientRole == role());
      allow create: if anyStaff()
        && request.resource.data.keys().hasOnly(['recipientUid', 'recipientRole', 'title', 'message', 'type', 'link', 'refId',
          'readBy', 'starredBy', 'createdByUid', 'createdByName', 'createdAt'])
        && (
          request.resource.data.createdByUid == request.auth.uid
          // Anonymous complaint alert: no sender recorded, HR only, complaint type only
          || (request.resource.data.createdByUid == null
              && request.resource.data.createdByName == ''
              && request.resource.data.recipientRole == 'hr'
              && request.resource.data.type == 'complaint')
        )
        && request.resource.data.readBy == []
        && request.resource.data.get('starredBy', []) == []
        && request.resource.data.title is string && request.resource.data.title.size() > 0 && request.resource.data.title.size() <= 200
        && request.resource.data.message is string && request.resource.data.message.size() <= 600
        && request.resource.data.link is string && request.resource.data.link.matches('/.*')
        && ((request.resource.data.recipientUid is string && request.resource.data.recipientRole == null)
          || (request.resource.data.recipientUid == null
            && (request.resource.data.recipientRole in ['director', 'finance', 'it', 'hr', 'operations', 'procurement', 'marketing']
              // Draft 0.21: a role made on the Roles page (e.g. Maintenance)
              || (request.resource.data.recipientRole is string && exists(roleDoc(request.resource.data.recipientRole))))));
      // Read, unread, star and hide (Draft 0.22): the recipient adds or removes only their own uid in readBy / starredBy / hiddenBy.
      allow update: if anyStaff() && (resource.data.recipientUid == request.auth.uid || resource.data.recipientRole == role())
        && changed().hasOnly(['readBy', 'starredBy', 'hiddenBy'])
        && onlyMine(resource.data.readBy, request.resource.data.readBy)
        && onlyMine(resource.data.get('starredBy', []), request.resource.data.get('starredBy', []))
        && onlyMine(resource.data.get('hiddenBy', []), request.resource.data.get('hiddenBy', []));
      // Draft 0.22: a notification sent to one person may be deleted by that person (Clear on the Notifications page).
      // Team notifications are never deleted (others still need them): they are hidden per person above.
      allow delete: if anyStaff() && resource.data.recipientUid == request.auth.uid;
    }

    // ================= HR: SOPs, Playbook, onboarding, complaints =================

    // sops/{key}. Everyone reads; HR and Directors edit and soft-delete (deleted: true). Never removed.
    match /sops/{sopKey} {
      allow read: if anyStaff();
      // Any SOP key: lower case, digits and dashes, 2 to 40 long (the first four keep their keys).
      allow create, update: if can('sops.edit') && sopKey.matches('^[a-z0-9][a-z0-9-]{1,39}$')
        && request.resource.data.updatedByUid == request.auth.uid
        && request.resource.data.steps is list && request.resource.data.steps.size() > 0
        && (!('title' in request.resource.data) || (request.resource.data.title is string
          && request.resource.data.title.size() > 0 && request.resource.data.title.size() <= 80))
        && (!('sub' in request.resource.data) || (request.resource.data.sub is string && request.resource.data.sub.size() <= 200))
        && (!('icon' in request.resource.data) || (request.resource.data.icon is string && request.resource.data.icon.size() <= 30))
        // Deleting is a soft delete with a reason.
        && (!('deleted' in request.resource.data) || (request.resource.data.deleted == true
          && request.resource.data.deleteReason is string && request.resource.data.deleteReason.size() > 0));
      allow delete: if false;
    }

    // playbook/businessModel and playbook/onboarding. Everyone reads; HR and Directors edit.
    match /playbook/{pageId} {
      allow read: if anyStaff();
      allow create, update: if can('playbook.edit') && pageId in ['businessModel', 'onboarding']
        && request.resource.data.updatedByUid == request.auth.uid;
      allow delete: if false;
    }

    // Onboarding ticks: each person writes their own; HR and Directors read everyone's.
    match /onboardingProgress/{uid} {
      allow read: if signedIn() && (request.auth.uid == uid || hrOrDir());
      allow create, update: if anyStaff() && request.auth.uid == uid
        && newKeysOnly(['ticks', 'updatedAt']) && request.resource.data.ticks is map;
      allow delete: if false;
    }

    // complaints/{id}, kind 'staff' (any staff -> HR) or 'director' (HR -> Directors). The parent holds only ref, kind,
    // date, createdAt and status/read (plus fromId on a named staff complaint); the text is in private/main.
    // An anonymous staff complaint has no fromId or fromName anywhere.
    match /complaints/{id} {
      // HR reads everything. Directors read only Director complaints (never staff complaints).
      allow read: if (isHR() && (resource.data.kind == 'staff' || resource.data.fromId == request.auth.uid)) || (isDirector() && resource.data.kind == 'director');
      // The sender of a named complaint follows it under My complaints.
      allow read: if signedIn() && resource.data.kind == 'staff' && resource.data.get('fromId', null) == request.auth.uid;
      // An anonymous sender's browser keeps the (random) id and reads only the status.
      allow get: if anyStaff() && resource.data.kind == 'staff' && resource.data.anonymous == true;
      allow create: if anyStaff() && request.resource.data.kind == 'staff' && request.resource.data.status == 'new'
        && newKeysOnly(['ref', 'kind', 'date', 'createdAt', 'status', 'anonymous', 'fromId'])
        && ((request.resource.data.anonymous == false && request.resource.data.fromId == request.auth.uid)
          || (request.resource.data.anonymous == true && !('fromId' in request.resource.data)));
      // Director complaints: HR sends (Directors too, so the form can be tried out).
      allow create: if hrOrDir() && request.resource.data.kind == 'director' && request.resource.data.read == false
        && newKeysOnly(['ref', 'kind', 'date', 'createdAt', 'read', 'fromId']) && request.resource.data.get('fromId', null) == request.auth.uid;
      // Draft 0.25: HR opening a New staff complaint marks it Read by HR; the only change ever made to a staff complaint.
      allow update: if isHR() && resource.data.kind == 'staff' && resource.data.status == 'new'
        && changed().hasOnly(['status', 'readAt', 'readBy'])
        && request.resource.data.status == 'read' && request.resource.data.readBy == request.auth.uid;
      // Draft 0.28 (Khairul): HR moves a staff complaint to Read by HR, In review or Closed (Reopen = back to In review).
      allow update: if isHR() && resource.data.kind == 'staff'
        && changed().hasOnly(['status', 'statusAt', 'statusBy'])
        && request.resource.data.status in ['read', 'review', 'closed'] && request.resource.data.statusBy == request.auth.uid;
      // Only a Director opening a Director complaint marks it read.
      allow update: if isDirector() && resource.data.kind == 'director'
        && changed().hasOnly(['read', 'readAt', 'readBy', 'status'])
        && request.resource.data.read == true && request.resource.data.readBy == request.auth.uid
        && (!changed().hasAny(['status']) || request.resource.data.status == 'read');
      // Draft 0.30: the Directors move a Director complaint to Read by the Directors, In review or Closed (Reopen = In review).
      allow update: if isDirector() && resource.data.kind == 'director'
        && changed().hasOnly(['status', 'statusAt', 'statusBy'])
        && request.resource.data.status in ['read', 'review', 'closed'] && request.resource.data.statusBy == request.auth.uid;
      allow delete: if false;
      // Draft 0.28 (Khairul): the conversation with the sender. HR reads all; the named sender reads theirs; an anonymous
      // sender's browser reads by the (random) id, like the status. HR writes any time (a closing note goes with the Close);
      // the NAMED sender writes back while it isn't Closed. Text up to 2000 characters (or photos only), never changed.
      match /thread/{tid} {
        allow read: if (isHR() && complaintNow(id).kind == 'staff')
          || (signedIn() && complaintNow(id).kind == 'staff' && complaintNow(id).get('fromId', null) == request.auth.uid)
          || (anyStaff() && complaintNow(id).kind == 'staff' && complaintNow(id).get('anonymous', false) == true);
        allow create: if complaintNow(id).kind == 'staff'
          && newKeysOnly(['text', 'by', 'byName', 'byUid', 'closing', 'imageIds', 'createdAt'])
          && request.resource.data.text is string && request.resource.data.text.size() <= 2000
          && (request.resource.data.text.size() > 0
            || (request.resource.data.get('imageIds', []) is list && request.resource.data.get('imageIds', []).size() > 0))
          && request.resource.data.get('imageIds', []).size() <= 5
          && request.resource.data.byUid == request.auth.uid
          && ((isHR() && request.resource.data.by == 'hr')
            || (request.resource.data.by == 'sender' && complaintNow(id).get('fromId', null) == request.auth.uid
                && complaintNow(id).status != 'closed' && !('closing' in request.resource.data)));
        // Draft 0.29: a Director complaint's conversation is between HR and the Directors
        allow read: if dirSide(id);
        // Draft 0.30: a closing note (closing) comes only from the Directors; HR can't write once it is Closed.
        allow create: if dirSide(id)
          && newKeysOnly(['text', 'by', 'byName', 'byUid', 'imageIds', 'closing', 'createdAt'])
          && request.resource.data.text is string && request.resource.data.text.size() <= 2000
          && (request.resource.data.text.size() > 0
            || (request.resource.data.get('imageIds', []) is list && request.resource.data.get('imageIds', []).size() > 0))
          && request.resource.data.get('imageIds', []).size() <= 5
          && request.resource.data.byUid == request.auth.uid
          && ((isHR() && request.resource.data.by == 'hr' && complaintNow(id).get('status', '') != 'closed' && !('closing' in request.resource.data))
            || (isDirector() && request.resource.data.by == 'director'));
        allow update, delete: if false;
      }
      // Draft 0.28 (Khairul): photos. Read by the same people as the conversation. Added with the complaint by its sender
      // (an anonymous complaint: no uid, and only in the first 15 minutes after it was sent), or with a reply by HR or the
      // named sender (not once Closed). Each record is one image, at most ~700 KB of text.
      match /images/{img} {
        allow read: if (isHR() && complaintNow(id).kind == 'staff')
          || (signedIn() && complaintNow(id).kind == 'staff' && complaintNow(id).get('fromId', null) == request.auth.uid)
          || (anyStaff() && complaintNow(id).kind == 'staff' && complaintNow(id).get('anonymous', false) == true);
        allow create: if complaintNow(id).kind == 'staff'
          && newKeysOnly(['data', 'w', 'h', 'size', 'scope', 'threadId', 'byUid', 'createdAt'])
          && request.resource.data.data is string && request.resource.data.data.size() <= 700000
          && ((request.resource.data.scope == 'complaint' && !('threadId' in request.resource.data)
                && ((complaintNow(id).get('fromId', null) == request.auth.uid && request.resource.data.get('byUid', '') == request.auth.uid)
                  || (anyStaff() && complaintNow(id).get('anonymous', false) == true && !('byUid' in request.resource.data)
                      && request.time < complaintNow(id).createdAt + duration.value(15, 'm'))))
            || (request.resource.data.scope == 'thread' && request.resource.data.threadId is string
                && request.resource.data.get('byUid', '') == request.auth.uid
                && (isHR() || (complaintNow(id).get('fromId', null) == request.auth.uid && complaintNow(id).status != 'closed'))));
        // Draft 0.29: Director complaints: HR and Directors read and add photos (with the complaint or a reply)
        allow read: if dirSide(id);
        allow create: if dirSide(id)
          && newKeysOnly(['data', 'w', 'h', 'size', 'scope', 'threadId', 'byUid', 'createdAt'])
          && request.resource.data.data is string && request.resource.data.data.size() <= 700000
          && request.resource.data.get('byUid', '') == request.auth.uid
          && (request.resource.data.scope == 'complaint' || (request.resource.data.scope == 'thread' && request.resource.data.threadId is string));
        allow update, delete: if false;
      }
      // Draft 0.28 (Khairul): HR's own notes on a staff complaint; nobody else reads them.
      // Draft 0.30: the Directors' own notes on a Director complaint; HR never reads those.
      match /notes/{nid} {
        allow read: if (isHR() && complaintNow(id).kind == 'staff') || (isDirector() && complaintNow(id).kind == 'director');
        allow create: if ((isHR() && complaintNow(id).kind == 'staff') || (isDirector() && complaintNow(id).kind == 'director'))
          && newKeysOnly(['text', 'byName', 'byUid', 'createdAt'])
          && request.resource.data.text is string && request.resource.data.text.size() > 0 && request.resource.data.text.size() <= 2000
          && request.resource.data.byUid == request.auth.uid;
        allow update, delete: if false;
      }
      match /private/{docId} {
        allow read: if isHR() && complaintNow(id).kind == 'staff';
        allow read: if dirSide(id);
        // Draft 0.40 backup check: the HR sender reads their own private part by its own fromUid (no get() on the parent)
        allow read: if isHR() && resource.data.get('fromUid', null) == request.auth.uid;
        allow read: if signedIn() && complaintNow(id).kind == 'staff' && complaintNow(id).get('fromId', null) == request.auth.uid;
        // Written once, in the same transaction as the parent. Anonymous: no fromName.
        allow create: if docId == 'main' && anyStaff()
          && newKeysOnly(['subject', 'details', 'files', 'fromName', 'fromUid'])
          && (!('fromUid' in request.resource.data) || request.resource.data.fromUid == request.auth.uid)
          && ((complaintAfter(id).kind == 'staff'
                && (complaintAfter(id).anonymous == true ? !('fromName' in request.resource.data) && !('fromUid' in request.resource.data) : complaintAfter(id).fromId == request.auth.uid))
            || (complaintAfter(id).kind == 'director' && hrOrDir()));
        allow update, delete: if false;
      }
    }

    // ================= Procurement: New Owner Listings =================

    // newOwnerListings/{NL-0001}: one new unit from service agreement to Live. New Owner Listings Edit creates and edits;
    // anyone with the page ticked reads. Owner phone and email in private/main (editors; Operations with View read them).
    match /newOwnerListings/{id} {
      allow read: if listingViewer() || listingEditor();
      allow create: if listingEditor() && id.matches('NL-[0-9]{4,}')
        && request.resource.data.createdByUid == request.auth.uid
        && request.resource.data.status in ['inProgress', 'live'];
      allow update: if listingEditor()
        && !changed().hasAny(['createdByUid', 'createdByName', 'createdAt'])
        && request.resource.data.status in ['inProgress', 'live'];
      allow delete: if false;
      match /private/{docId} {
        allow read: if (listingEditor() || (opsRole() && listingViewer())) && docId == 'main';
        allow write: if listingEditor() && docId == 'main';
      }
    }

    // ================= Performance management (Stage 1+2 security/revision fixes, 3 Nov 2026) =================
    // performance.edit is not yet in presetFor()/PRESETS — until it's added, only the Director can write.
    // Everyone reads quarter config (deadlines, status) so excluded employees can be told why they see nothing further.
    function perfEdit() { return isDirector() || can('performance.edit'); }
    // By business rule, Director/HR (performance.edit) may edit or delete a quarter's configuration at any
    // lifecycle status, including finalized/archived — not restricted to draft. This is a deliberate choice,
    // not an oversight: editing a quarter that's already in progress can change what a later recalculation
    // produces, and deleting one does not cascade-delete its participants/evaluations/results (they stay
    // queryable by quarterId even without a parent quarter doc). setStatus() still only touches status+stamp.
    match /performanceQuarters/{id} {
      allow read: if anyStaff();
      allow create, update: if perfEdit();
      allow delete: if perfEdit();
    }

    // Participation rosters are readable by every staff member, not just the participant themselves: COH
    // evaluation requires every employee to see who else is eligible this quarter in order to rate them.
    match /performanceParticipants/{id} {
      allow read: if anyStaff();
      allow create, update: if isDirector() || can('performance.edit');
      allow delete: if false;
    }

    // COH questions: everyone reads (so they know what they're being rated on); only performance.edit changes them.
    // Confirmed business rule: COH questions are Director/HR only — not the generic performance.edit tick that
    // gates other Performance admin actions, since question wording is a Code of Conduct/HR policy matter.
    match /cohQuestions/{id} {
      allow read: if anyStaff();
      allow create, update: if hrOrDir();
      allow delete: if false;
    }

    // COH evaluations: evaluator identity is always visible to the evaluatee and to HR/Director (confirmed
    // requirement, not an anonymous system). The id itself (quarterId_evaluatorUid_evaluateeUid) stops one
    // evaluator from rating the same colleague twice under two different documents.
    // The SCORE is not on this document (see private/scores below) — by business rule, the person being rated
    // never sees the mark a specific evaluator gave them, only that the evaluation happened and who gave it.
    match /cohEvaluations/{id} {
      function evalDoc() { return /databases/$(database)/documents/cohEvaluations/$(id); }

      // Director and HR always see every evaluation (Team overview monitoring), regardless of whether they
      // hold the generic performance.edit tick — same confirmed business rule as cohQuestions above.
      // (resource == null && anyStaff()): getEvaluation() probes this exact id to check "have I already rated
      // this colleague" before the doc exists — without this clause that probe gets permission-denied instead
      // of a normal exists:false, breaking "Evaluate" the first time anyone opens a colleague.
      allow read: if (resource == null && anyStaff()) || isDirector() || isHR() || can('performance.edit')
        || resource.data.evaluatorId == request.auth.uid || resource.data.evaluateeId == request.auth.uid;
      allow create: if anyStaff() && request.resource.data.evaluatorId == request.auth.uid
        && request.resource.data.evaluateeId != request.auth.uid
        && id == request.resource.data.quarterId + '_' + request.resource.data.evaluatorId + '_' + request.resource.data.evaluateeId
        && request.resource.data.status == 'submitted'
        && !('ratings' in request.resource.data) && !('averageRating' in request.resource.data);
      // Resubmit: same pair, saved back as 'submitted'. Draft 0.34: also allowed from 'approved', so an evaluator can
      // answer questions added after they submitted; it then goes back to 'submitted' for HR/Director to review again.
      // The marks themselves are protected in private/scores below (earlier answers can't be dropped once approved).
      allow update: if anyStaff() && resource.data.evaluatorId == request.auth.uid && resource.data.status in ['submitted', 'approved']
        && request.resource.data.evaluatorId == resource.data.evaluatorId && request.resource.data.evaluateeId == resource.data.evaluateeId
        && request.resource.data.status == 'submitted'
        && !('ratings' in request.resource.data) && !('averageRating' in request.resource.data);
      // HR/Director approve: only the review fields change.
      allow update: if (isDirector() || can('performance.edit'))
        && changed().hasOnly(['status', 'reviewedBy', 'reviewedAt']) && request.resource.data.status == 'approved';
      allow delete: if false;

      // The actual marks: readable by the evaluator (it's their own input) and HR/Director (monitoring and
      // official score calculation, see results.js::cohScoreFor) — never by the evaluatee. Immutable once
      // written; a correction is a resubmit of the whole evaluation (both documents), not a patch here.
      // Draft 0.32: every check on the parent is null-safe. get() on a parent that doesn't exist yet errors (= deny),
      // which blocked every role without a separate way in (only Director, HR and Finance could evaluate).
      match /private/scores {
        // resource == null: the "have I rated this colleague yet" probe returns not-found instead of denied.
        allow read: if (resource == null && anyStaff())
          || isDirector() || isHR() || can('performance.edit')
          || (exists(evalDoc()) && get(evalDoc()).data.evaluatorId == request.auth.uid);
        // The parent and the scores are written in the same batch, so check the parent as it will be after the write.
        allow create: if anyStaff()
          && existsAfter(evalDoc())
          && getAfter(evalDoc()).data.evaluatorId == request.auth.uid
          && request.resource.data.ratings is list && request.resource.data.averageRating is number;
        allow update: if anyStaff()
          && exists(evalDoc())
          && get(evalDoc()).data.evaluatorId == request.auth.uid
          // Draft 0.34: while 'submitted' the evaluator may change anything; once 'approved' only by ADDING answers
          // (new questions), and the evaluation must go back to 'submitted' in the same write for re-review.
          && (get(evalDoc()).data.status == 'submitted'
            || (get(evalDoc()).data.status == 'approved'
                && getAfter(evalDoc()).data.status == 'submitted'
                && request.resource.data.ratings.size() > resource.data.ratings.size()))
          && request.resource.data.ratings is list && request.resource.data.averageRating is number;
        allow delete: if false;
      }
    }

    // KPI assignments: HR/Director create and edit; the employee and HR/Director read.
    // (resource == null && anyStaff()) lets a getDoc() that's just probing "does this exist yet" return
    // exists:false instead of permission-denied — without it, resource.data errors on a missing document and
    // the whole rule denies, which is what was breaking the KPI page for a brand-new, never-submitted task.
    match /kpiAssignments/{id} {
      allow read: if (resource == null && anyStaff()) || isDirector() || resource.data.employeeId == request.auth.uid;
      allow create, update: if isDirector();
      allow delete: if false;
    }

    // KPI submissions: the employee submits their own self-assessment (status 'submitted', no final rating set
    // yet); only HR/Director can set finalApprovedRating / reviewerId, and only by changing review fields.
    // Draft 0.31: Director can also reopen done KPIs and send back for discussion.
    match /kpiSubmissions/{id} {
      allow read: if (resource == null && anyStaff()) || isDirector() || resource.data.employeeId == request.auth.uid;
      // The employee submits or resubmits their own self-assessment, but never once it's already been
      // done (matches the KPI.vue UI, which hides the submit form at that point) — otherwise
      // an employee could write status back to 'submitted' with nulled-out review fields and erase a
      // reviewer's decision.
      allow create, update: if (resource == null || (resource.data.employeeId == request.auth.uid && resource.data.status != 'done'))
        && request.resource.data.employeeId == request.auth.uid
        && request.resource.data.status == 'submitted'
        && request.resource.data.get('finalApprovedRating', null) == null
        && request.resource.data.get('reviewerId', null) == null;
      // Director review and rating: provide rating/comments or approve/send back.
      allow update: if isDirector()
        && changed().hasOnly(['status', 'revisedRating', 'finalApprovedRating', 'reviewerId', 'reviewerComments', 'reviewReason',
          'directorRating', 'directorComments', 'directorId', 'ratedAt', 'discussionStatus', 'reviewedAt', 'history']);
      // Director can reopen a done KPI and send it back for discussion (allows re-rating after approval).
      allow update: if isDirector()
        && resource.data.status == 'done'
        && request.resource.data.status == 'discussionRequested'
        && changed().hasOnly(['status', 'directorRating', 'directorComments', 'directorId', 'ratedAt', 'discussionStatus', 'history']);
      // The employee's own discussion-status flip, set alongside their replies.
      allow update: if resource.data.employeeId == request.auth.uid && changed().hasOnly(['discussionStatus']);
      allow delete: if false;
    }

    // KPI conversation threads: complete discussion history for each KPI.
    // Only the assigned employee and director can access.
    // Draft 0.32: (resource == null && anyStaff()) so the chat's "is there a thread yet" probe isn't denied.
    match /kpiConversations/{id} {
      allow read: if (resource == null && anyStaff()) || isDirector() || resource.data.employeeId == request.auth.uid;
      allow create: if isDirector() && request.resource.data.assignmentId is string
        && request.resource.data.employeeId is string && request.resource.data.directorId is string
        && request.resource.data.messages is list && request.resource.data.status == 'active';
      allow update: if (isDirector() || resource.data.employeeId == request.auth.uid)
        && request.resource.data.messages is list;
      allow delete: if false;
    }

    // KPI discussion threads (deprecated): kept for backwards compatibility.
    match /kpiDiscussions/{id} {
      allow read: if (resource == null && anyStaff()) || isDirector() || resource.data.employeeId == request.auth.uid;
      allow create: if isDirector() && request.resource.data.submissionId is string && request.resource.data.employeeId is string
        && request.resource.data.directorId is string && request.resource.data.thread is list && request.resource.data.status == 'active';
      allow update: if (isDirector() || resource.data.employeeId == request.auth.uid) && request.resource.data.thread is list;
      allow delete: if false;
    }

    // Discussion requests: the employee who raised it, and HR/Director, read and resolve.
    match /performanceDiscussions/{id} {
      allow read: if (resource == null && anyStaff()) || isDirector() || can('performance.edit') || resource.data.employeeId == request.auth.uid;
      allow create: if request.resource.data.employeeId == request.auth.uid && request.resource.data.status == 'requested';
      allow update: if isDirector() || can('performance.edit');
      allow delete: if false;
    }

    // TMS performance snapshots: only HR/Director sync and approve (server-side TMS credentials never touch the
    // frontend — this just writes the result). The employee reads their own; isFinal is never flipped back to false.
    match /performanceTmsSnapshots/{id} {
      allow read: if (resource == null && anyStaff()) || isDirector() || can('performance.edit') || resource.data.employeeId == request.auth.uid;
      allow create, update: if (isDirector() || can('performance.edit')) && (resource == null || resource.data.get('isFinal', false) != true);
      allow delete: if false;
    }

    // Final combined results, and the Stage 2 revision trail. Nobody — Director included — can write once
    // approvalStatus is 'finalized', EXCEPT the one deliberate correction path: Director, going straight from
    // 'finalized' to 'pendingApproval', bumping revisionNumber by exactly 1 and recording who/why. The app
    // always writes a revisions/{rev} snapshot of the pre-correction values (results.js::requestCorrection)
    // before this write, so a correction is never silently applied over the original finalized numbers.
    match /performanceResults/{id} {
      allow read: if (resource == null && anyStaff()) || isDirector() || can('performance.edit') || resource.data.employeeId == request.auth.uid;
      allow create, update: if (isDirector() || can('performance.edit'))
        && (resource == null || resource.data.get('approvalStatus', 'draft') != 'finalized');
      allow update: if isDirector() && resource.data.get('approvalStatus', 'draft') == 'finalized'
        && request.resource.data.approvalStatus == 'pendingApproval'
        && request.resource.data.revisionNumber == resource.data.get('revisionNumber', 1) + 1
        && request.resource.data.get('revisionReason', '') is string && request.resource.data.get('revisionReason', '').size() > 0
        && request.resource.data.get('correctedBy', '') == request.auth.uid;
      allow delete: if false;

      // One immutable snapshot per revision, written right before the correction above.
      match /revisions/{rev} {
        allow read: if isDirector() || can('performance.edit') || get(/databases/$(database)/documents/performanceResults/$(id)).data.employeeId == request.auth.uid;
        allow create: if isDirector();
        allow update, delete: if false;
      }
    }

    // ================= Agreements (Draft 0.14, 0.15) =================
    function agreementAdmin() { return can('agreementSetup.view'); }

    // Form fields, formulas and column-only fields. Archived, never deleted.
    match /agreementForms/{id} {
      allow read: if anyStaff();
      allow create: if agreementAdmin() && request.resource.data.name is string && request.resource.data.fields is list
        && request.resource.data.createdBy == request.auth.uid;
      allow update: if agreementAdmin() && request.resource.data.fields is list && request.resource.data.createdBy == resource.data.createdBy;
      allow delete: if false;
    }

    // Uploaded agreement PDFs (the file itself is in Drive), their versions and where each field prints.
    match /agreementTemplates/{id} {
      allow read: if anyStaff();
      allow create: if agreementAdmin() && request.resource.data.formId is string && request.resource.data.mappings is list
        && request.resource.data.createdBy == request.auth.uid;
      allow update: if agreementAdmin() && request.resource.data.mappings is list
        && request.resource.data.formId == resource.data.formId && request.resource.data.createdBy == resource.data.createdBy;
      allow delete: if false;
    }

    // One record per filled-in form. Everyone reads and writes; the form and the creator never change. Archived, never deleted.
    match /agreementRecords/{id} {
      allow read: if anyStaff();
      allow create: if anyStaff() && request.resource.data.formId is string && request.resource.data.values is map
        && request.resource.data.status in ['draft', 'submitted', 'completed', 'archived'] && request.resource.data.createdBy == request.auth.uid;
      allow update: if anyStaff() && request.resource.data.values is map
        && request.resource.data.status in ['draft', 'submitted', 'completed', 'archived']
        && request.resource.data.formId == resource.data.formId && request.resource.data.createdBy == resource.data.createdBy;
      allow delete: if false;
    }

    // Master files: Word / Google Docs kept in Drive ("Master File (DO NOT EDIT)"). Only the record of them is here.
    match /agreementMasters/{id} {
      allow read: if anyStaff();
      allow create: if agreementAdmin() && request.resource.data.docId is string && request.resource.data.createdBy == request.auth.uid;
      allow update: if agreementAdmin() && request.resource.data.docId is string && request.resource.data.createdBy == resource.data.createdBy;
      allow delete: if false;
    }

    // Fill-in links for outside people; the link name is the document id (/f/{slug}). Passwords are stored only as
    // salt + SHA-256. "Anyone" links need Agreement Setup; any staff member may make a personal link for one record.
    // Turned off or deleted (records already sent in stay). The Apps Script records submissions (it writes as the company account).
    match /agreementLinks/{slug} {
      function linkOk() {
        return slug.matches('[a-z0-9-]{3,60}') && request.resource.data.slug == slug
          && request.resource.data.kind in ['open', 'personal'] && request.resource.data.formId is string
          && request.resource.data.get('passHash', '') is string;
      }
      allow read: if anyStaff();
      allow create: if anyStaff() && linkOk() && request.resource.data.createdBy == request.auth.uid
        && (agreementAdmin() || (request.resource.data.kind == 'personal' && request.resource.data.recordId is string));
      allow update: if anyStaff() && linkOk() && request.resource.data.kind == resource.data.kind
        && request.resource.data.formId == resource.data.formId && request.resource.data.createdBy == resource.data.createdBy
        && (agreementAdmin() || resource.data.kind == 'personal');
      // Agreement Setup deletes any link; other staff only the personal links they made.
      allow delete: if anyStaff() && (agreementAdmin() || (resource.data.kind == 'personal' && resource.data.createdBy == request.auth.uid));
    }

    // Saved table layouts (columns, widths, filters). Shared by everyone.
    match /agreementViews/{id} {
      allow read, delete: if anyStaff();
      allow create, update: if anyStaff() && request.resource.data.formId is string && request.resource.data.view is map;
    }

    // History of generated PDFs. Written once by the person who made it.
    match /generatedAgreements/{id} {
      allow read: if anyStaff();
      allow create: if anyStaff() && request.resource.data.by == request.auth.uid && request.resource.data.recordId is string
        && request.resource.data.fileId is string;
      allow update, delete: if false;
    }

    // ================= Booking numbers (Booking Form, Create booking and the Willow Booking Details bulk upload) =================
    // One counter per property prefix gives the next booking no. (DM-014). The Reservation Lodgment form is gone; offline bookings are the one booking record.
    function lodgeStaff() { return finOrDir() || isOps() || can('bookingForms.view'); }
    match /lodgmentCounters/{prefix} {
      allow read: if lodgeStaff();
      allow create, update: if lodgeStaff() && request.resource.data.next is int;
      allow delete: if false;
    }

    // ================= Salary advances (Draft 0.42, 5 Nov 2026) =================
    // Data shape and flow: src/pages/HR/advances.js.
    function hrPath(uid)    { return /databases/$(database)/documents/staffHR/$(uid); }
    function limitPath(uid) { return /databases/$(database)/documents/advanceLimits/$(uid); }
    function advPath(id)    { return /databases/$(database)/documents/advances/$(id); }
    // HR and Directors keep the details; HR can't change their own (a Director does).
    function hrDetailsEditor(uid) { return isDirector() || (isHR() && uid != request.auth.uid); }

    // IC, position and monthly salary. Never readable by the staff member.
    match /staffHR/{uid} {
      allow read: if hrOrDir();
      allow create, update: if hrDetailsEditor(uid)
        && request.resource.data.keys().hasOnly(['ic', 'position', 'salary', 'updatedAt', 'updatedBy', 'updatedByName'])
        && request.resource.data.ic is string && request.resource.data.position is string
        && request.resource.data.salary is number && request.resource.data.salary >= 0
        && request.resource.data.updatedBy == request.auth.uid
        && getAfter(limitPath(uid)).data.limit == request.resource.data.salary * 0.5;
      allow delete: if false;
    }
    // The advance limit (50% of the salary): the only part the person reads.
    match /advanceLimits/{uid} {
      allow read: if signedIn() && (request.auth.uid == uid || hrOrDir());
      allow create, update: if hrDetailsEditor(uid)
        && request.resource.data.keys().hasOnly(['limit', 'updatedAt'])
        && request.resource.data.limit == getAfter(hrPath(uid)).data.salary * 0.5;
      allow delete: if false;
    }

    match /advances/{id} {
      function grows()     { return request.resource.data.history is list && request.resource.data.history.size() == resource.data.history.size() + 1; }
      function from(a, b)  { return resource.data.status == a && request.resource.data.status == b; }
      function onlyKeys(k) { return changed().hasOnly(['status', 'history', 'updatedAt'].concat(k)); }
      // HR moves a request on, never their own.
      function mover()     { return isHR() && resource.data.uid != request.auth.uid; }
      function limitOfOwner() { return get(hrPath(resource.data.uid)).data.salary * 0.5; }
      function sub(name, d)   { return /databases/$(database)/documents/advances/$(id)/$(name)/$(d); }
      function mine()         { return signedIn() && resource.data.uid == request.auth.uid; }

      allow read: if hrOrDir() || (signedIn() && resource.data.uid == request.auth.uid);
      // Staff: their own request, Submitted, within 50% of the salary HR entered (no salary = refused). Not interns.
      allow create: if anyStaff() && request.resource.data.uid == request.auth.uid
        && get(myRecord()).data.get('intern', false) != true
        && newKeysOnly(['ref', 'uid', 'name', 'amount', 'reason', 'neededBy', 'status', 'history', 'createdAt', 'updatedAt'])
        && request.resource.data.status == 'submitted'
        && request.resource.data.ref is string && request.resource.data.name is string
        && request.resource.data.amount is number && request.resource.data.amount > 0
        && exists(hrPath(request.auth.uid))
        && request.resource.data.amount <= get(hrPath(request.auth.uid)).data.salary * 0.5
        && request.resource.data.reason is string && request.resource.data.reason.size() > 0 && request.resource.data.reason.size() <= 1000
        && (!('neededBy' in request.resource.data) || request.resource.data.neededBy is string)
        && request.resource.data.history is list && request.resource.data.history.size() == 1;
      // HR: make the form for a staff member (byHR), straight at Reviewed; form/main and signatureUses in the same save.
      allow create: if isHR() && request.resource.data.uid != request.auth.uid
        && request.resource.data.byHR == true
        && get(/databases/$(database)/documents/users/$(request.resource.data.uid)).data.get('intern', false) != true
        && newKeysOnly(['ref', 'uid', 'name', 'amount', 'reason', 'description', 'status', 'byHR', 'approvedAmount', 'reviewedAt',
          'reviewedBy', 'reviewedByName', 'reviewedDate', 'chloeTold', 'history', 'createdAt', 'updatedAt'])
        && request.resource.data.status == 'reviewed'
        && request.resource.data.ref is string && request.resource.data.name is string
        && request.resource.data.amount is number && request.resource.data.amount > 0
        && request.resource.data.approvedAmount == request.resource.data.amount
        && exists(hrPath(request.resource.data.uid))
        && request.resource.data.amount <= get(hrPath(request.resource.data.uid)).data.salary * 0.5
        && request.resource.data.reason is string && request.resource.data.reason.size() > 0 && request.resource.data.reason.size() <= 1000
        && (!('description' in request.resource.data) || (request.resource.data.description is string && request.resource.data.description.size() <= 1000))
        && request.resource.data.reviewedBy == request.auth.uid
        && request.resource.data.chloeTold.by == request.auth.uid
        && request.resource.data.history is list && request.resource.data.history.size() == 1
        && existsAfter(sub('form', 'main'))
        && existsAfter(/databases/$(database)/documents/signatureUses/$(id));
      // Staff: withdraw while Submitted.
      allow update: if mine() && from('submitted', 'withdrawn')
        && onlyKeys(['withdrawnAt']) && grows();
      // HR: reject with a reason, at Submitted or Signed.
      allow update: if mover() && (from('submitted', 'rejected') || from('signed', 'rejected')) && grows()
        && onlyKeys(['rejectReason', 'rejectedAt', 'rejectedBy', 'rejectedByName'])
        && request.resource.data.rejectReason is string && request.resource.data.rejectReason.size() > 0
        && request.resource.data.rejectedBy == request.auth.uid;
      // HR: review (within the limit, Director told; form and signature-use line written in the same batch).
      allow update: if mover() && from('submitted', 'reviewed') && grows()
        && onlyKeys(['approvedAmount', 'reviewedAt', 'reviewedBy', 'reviewedByName', 'reviewedDate', 'chloeTold'])
        && request.resource.data.approvedAmount is number && request.resource.data.approvedAmount > 0
        && request.resource.data.approvedAmount <= limitOfOwner()
        && request.resource.data.reviewedBy == request.auth.uid
        && request.resource.data.chloeTold.by == request.auth.uid
        && existsAfter(sub('form', 'main'))
        && existsAfter(/databases/$(database)/documents/signatureUses/$(id));
      // Staff: sign (drawn on screen or a photo of the signed paper form, saved in signed/main in the same batch).
      allow update: if mine() && from('reviewed', 'signed') && grows()
        && resource.data.get('byHR', false) != true
        && onlyKeys(['signMethod', 'signedAt'])
        && request.resource.data.signMethod in ['drawn', 'upload']
        && existsAfter(sub('signed', 'main'));
      // HR: signed outside the PMS; the fully signed document (signed/copy) is required.
      allow update: if mover() && from('reviewed', 'signed') && grows()
        && onlyKeys(['signMethod', 'signedAt', 'signedCopyAt'])
        && request.resource.data.signMethod == 'outside'
        && existsAfter(sub('signed', 'main')) && existsAfter(sub('signed', 'copy'));
      // HR: add or replace the fully signed document later (status unchanged).
      allow update: if mover() && resource.data.status in ['signed', 'approved', 'paid']
        && request.resource.data.status == resource.data.status && grows()
        && onlyKeys(['signedCopyAt']) && existsAfter(sub('signed', 'copy'));
      // HR: approve (pending payment), then paid with type, date and screenshot.
      allow update: if mover() && from('signed', 'approved') && grows()
        && onlyKeys(['approvedAt', 'approvedBy', 'approvedByName'])
        && request.resource.data.approvedBy == request.auth.uid;
      allow update: if mover() && from('approved', 'paid') && grows()
        && onlyKeys(['paidDate', 'paymentType', 'paidAt', 'paidBy', 'paidByName'])
        && request.resource.data.paidDate is string && request.resource.data.paidBy == request.auth.uid
        && request.resource.data.paymentType in ['tng', 'bank']
        && existsAfter(sub('payment', 'main'));
      allow delete: if false;

      // The form as reviewed (IC, salary, Director's signature): the staff member, HR and Directors. Written once, at review.
      match /form/{doc} {
        allow read: if hrOrDir() || (signedIn() && get(advPath(id)).data.uid == request.auth.uid);
        allow create: if isHR() && doc == 'main'
          && ((!exists(advPath(id)) && getAfter(advPath(id)).data.byHR == true)
            || get(advPath(id)).data.status == 'submitted')
          && getAfter(advPath(id)).data.uid != request.auth.uid
          && getAfter(advPath(id)).data.status == 'reviewed'
          && request.resource.data.uid == getAfter(advPath(id)).data.uid
          && request.resource.data.createdBy == request.auth.uid
          && request.resource.data.signature == get(/databases/$(database)/documents/signatures/director).data.image;
        allow update, delete: if false;
      }
      // How it was signed (main) and the fully signed document (copy): the staff member, HR and Directors read.
      // main: the staff member when signing (drawn / upload), or HR marking it signed outside. Written once.
      // copy: HR only, required with 'outside', can be added or replaced while signed, approved or paid.
      match /signed/{doc} {
        function isImage() { return request.resource.data.image is string && request.resource.data.image.size() < 700000; }
        allow read: if hrOrDir() || (signedIn() && get(advPath(id)).data.uid == request.auth.uid);
        allow create: if doc == 'main' && request.resource.data.by == request.auth.uid
          && get(advPath(id)).data.status == 'reviewed' && getAfter(advPath(id)).data.status == 'signed'
          && ((get(advPath(id)).data.uid == request.auth.uid && request.resource.data.method in ['drawn', 'upload'] && isImage())
            || (isHR() && get(advPath(id)).data.uid != request.auth.uid && request.resource.data.method == 'outside'));
        allow create, update: if doc == 'copy' && isHR() && get(advPath(id)).data.uid != request.auth.uid
          && request.resource.data.by == request.auth.uid && isImage()
          && getAfter(advPath(id)).data.status in ['signed', 'approved', 'paid'];
        allow delete: if false;
      }
      // Payment screenshot: HR writes it with Paid; HR and Directors read (for the record, not the staff member).
      match /payment/{doc} {
        allow read: if hrOrDir();
        allow create: if isHR() && doc == 'main' && get(advPath(id)).data.uid != request.auth.uid
          && request.resource.data.by == request.auth.uid
          && request.resource.data.image is string && request.resource.data.image.size() < 700000
          && get(advPath(id)).data.status == 'approved' && getAfter(advPath(id)).data.status == 'paid';
        allow update, delete: if false;
      }
      // HR's own notes. HR writes; HR and Directors read (HR never on their own request).
      match /notes/{noteId} {
        allow read: if isDirector() || (isHR() && get(advPath(id)).data.uid != request.auth.uid);
        allow create: if isHR() && get(advPath(id)).data.uid != request.auth.uid
          && request.resource.data.keys().hasOnly(['text', 'byName', 'byUid', 'createdAt'])
          && request.resource.data.byUid == request.auth.uid
          && request.resource.data.text is string && request.resource.data.text.size() > 0 && request.resource.data.text.size() <= 1000;
        allow update, delete: if false;
      }
    }

    // The Director's saved signature (default Miss Chloe), put on approved forms. HR uploads it for her; Directors may too.
    match /signatures/{id} {
      allow read: if hrOrDir();
      allow create, update: if hrOrDir() && id == 'director'
        && request.resource.data.keys().hasOnly(['signerName', 'image', 'updatedAt', 'updatedBy', 'updatedByName'])
        && request.resource.data.signerName is string && request.resource.data.signerName.size() > 0 && request.resource.data.signerName.size() <= 100
        && request.resource.data.image is string && request.resource.data.image.size() < 700000
        && request.resource.data.updatedBy == request.auth.uid;
      allow delete: if false;
    }
    // One line per form that carries the signature (id = the advance). Written with the approval, never changed.
    match /signatureUses/{id} {
      allow read: if hrOrDir();
      allow create: if isHR()
        && request.resource.data.keys().hasOnly(['advanceId', 'ref', 'staffName', 'signerName', 'createdBy', 'createdByName', 'at'])
        && request.resource.data.advanceId == id && request.resource.data.createdBy == request.auth.uid
        && ((!exists(advPath(id)) && getAfter(advPath(id)).data.byHR == true) || get(advPath(id)).data.status == 'submitted')
        && getAfter(advPath(id)).data.status == 'reviewed';
      allow update, delete: if false;
    }

  }
}
